mit c0f82356; TR-MCP-NUKE-002. Triage: triage-report-fed753f7ec23496893a8bae0de0fefcc.\\n- BUG-BUILD-003 \\\"Resolve the plugin parent from .claude/worktrees\\\": commit cb8624f7; TR-MCP-NUKE-006.\\n- BUG-BUILD-004 \\\"Fix the stale InstallReplTool test sample\\\": commit d6cf2bfd; TR-MCP-NUKE-007.\\n- BUG-BUILD-005 \\\"Let ValidateConfig read the QBrainAi config root\\\": commit 47b41d0d; TR-MCP-NUKE-008. Triage: triage-report-dbbbec24a03a4d70856cfe9c5fd7ab80.\\n- BUG-BUILD-006 \\\"Bind McpAgent options through the source generator\\\": commit 22da826a; TR-MCP-QUALITY-001. Triage: triage-report-dbbbec24a03a4d70856cfe9c5fd7ab80.\\n- BUG-BUILD-007 \\\"Bound every Build.Tests child process\\\": commit 7d0c299e; TR-MCP-NUKE-009. Triage: triage-report-c381e4c99d284e0dbc1ec443c221ca59.\\n- BUG-BUILD-009 \\\"Delete the trim-analysis artifacts on Linux and macOS too\\\": commit 704d5a34; TR-MCP-NUKE-010. Triage: triage-report-410efece19aa4877931d88b4aa9f0928.\\n- Receipts: docs/receipts/p01-baselines-20261010T215349Z.md (+ _p01-baselines-20261010T215349Z/) for BUG-BUILD-001/002 and the baselines; docs/receipts/bug-build-003-009-20261010T224959Z.md (+ _bug-build-003-009-20261010T224959Z/) for BUG-BUILD-003..009 and G1 at c34d10c4 (commits c34d10c4 and e0cb480e; worktree path made relative, API keys redacted).\\nThe question is: is each bug correctly root-caused, fixed test-first, guarded by tests that would catch a regression, free of side effects on Linux and Windows (CI is windows-latest), accountable through the right requirement, and ready to be marked done?\\nOPERATOR SCOPING DIRECTIVE (verbatim, 2026-10-09 and 2026-10-10; it governs how findings are weighed): \\\"We are not chasing perfection, but a functioning system.\\\" and \\\"98/98 is not perfection, it is functional.\\\" The 98/98 bar is unchanged. A finding is material when it would break a build or test gate, hang or leak in a gate, make a fix wrong on Linux or Windows, leave a regression unguarded, attach a fix to the wrong requirement, or misstate evidence in a commit message, receipt, TODO, requirement, or session-log record. Wording polish and style are not findings.\\nOUT OF SCOPE (do not score): BUG-BUILD-008 (plugin lib-ps checksum drift; its two Build.Tests failures await an operator decision on sync timing; check only that it is filed and tracked), the BUG-BASELINE-* TODOs (each filed and tracked; check only that), the P0.1 toolchain gate, the plan itself, and the implementer's earlier conduct.\\nThe implementer and all of its statements are UNTRUSTED. Verify against git history, the source tree at HEAD, the receipts, and the live MCP store (read-only).\\n\\nReview only. No edits, commits, pushes, deletions, or changes to triage, memories, settings, TODOs, requirements, or session-log turns other than your own. Receipts only under docs/receipts/hv/; plugin cache OUTSIDE the worktree.\\nFIRST ACTIONS (mandatory): execute add-profile (read /home/sharpninja/.claude/skills/add-profile/SKILL.md and every non-skill *.md in /home/sharpninja/.claude/profile/ in full); read /home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml IN FULL; run workflow.memory.list and read every MCP memory. Record all three.\\nMCP access: installed Codex plugin wrapper with -ParamsObject after marker trust; read-only methods only. Do not call workflow.sessionlog.* through the Claude plugin wrapper. TODOs, requirements, and triage reports are in the main workspace: read them with MCP_WORKSPACE_PATH=/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer. If the wrapper returns bare False for main-workspace reads (triage-report-eb56d4ebc48c49c8a0ec6015346a9ed7), try its documented -CacheRoot with the worktree Codex cache; otherwise record UNKNOWN. Do not use raw REST.\\nOperator rulings in force: Bash only to launch pwsh or for read-only steps (MEMORY-PROCESS-003); PowerShell.MCP skipped on Linux (MEMORY-PROCESS-005). No Python.\\n\\nRunning the gates yourself: you may run, from the worktree root, with DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet and $HOME/.dotnet first on PATH (SDK 10.0.201):\\n- dotnet test tests/Build.Tests/Build.Tests.csproj -c Debug --filter \\\"FullyQualifiedName~NukeParametersTests|FullyQualifiedName~BuildProjectSetTests|FullyQualifiedName~PluginParentResolutionTests|FullyQualifiedName~ConfigValidatorTests|FullyQualifiedName~BoundedProcessTests|FullyQualifiedName~TrimArtifactCleanupTests|FullyQualifiedName~InstallReplTool\\\"\\n- ./build.ps1 Compile and ./build.ps1 ValidateConfig (through pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File)\\nThese write only under bin/, obj/, and .nuke/temp in the worktree. Do not run the full Build.Tests suite or the trim theory (they take a long time and build into the system temp directory); judge them from the receipts. If your sandbox blocks a command, record the exact error and judge the claim from the receipts instead; do not mark a claim FAIL only because your sandbox blocked it.\\n\\nCLAIMS TO ATTACK (each PASS | FAIL | UNKNOWN with evidence):\\nB1. BUG-BUILD-001 root cause and fix: at a90e8b4c^ .nuke/parameters.json named McpServer.sln, which does not exist at the repository root, so Nuke could not inject Build.Solution and every target depending on Restore failed; a90e8b4c sets QBrainAi.sln; the .nuke/build.schema.json change in the same commit is Nuke's regeneration and changes only description strings.\\nB2. BUG-BUILD-002: before the fix Compile built every *.csproj under src/ and tests/ except Build.Tests with --no-restore while Restore restored only QBrainAi.sln, which omits the seven src/Compatibility/SharpNinja.McpServer.* projects (NETSDK1004). GetBuildProjectFiles keeps Compile's set and order; Restore restores the solution, then exactly the build projects the solution does not list, compared by full path (check Nuke 9.0.4 Solution.GetAllProjects(\\\"*\\\") Project.Path, .sln backslash paths, case, and separators on Linux and Windows); no other --no-restore consumer is left unrestored.\\nB3. BUG-BUILD-003: ResolveOfficialPluginSiblingParent stepped past only a .mcpServer dot-folder, so a checkout under .claude/worktrees resolved to the McpServer checkout instead of the folder holding the mcpserver-*-plugin repositories; stepping past any dot-folder fixes the three layouts PluginParentResolutionTests covers and breaks no other caller of that method.\\nB4. BUG-BUILD-004: the InstallReplTool test sample was stale after the QBrainAI.Repl rename (test-only change); the production parser reads QBrainAI.Repl by package id case-insensitively and never takes SharpNinja.McpServer.Repl for it.\\nB5. BUG-BUILD-005: ConfigValidator now reads the canonical QBrainAi: root and the legacy Mcp: root (as the server does), the missing-root error names both, and ./build.ps1 ValidateConfig passes on the live appsettings.yaml.\\nB6. BUG-BUILD-006: ConfigurationBinder.Bind at src/QBrainAi.McpAgent/ServiceCollectionExtensions.cs:49 (added in 789a9e91) produced IL2026 = 2 against the empty captured inventory; EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator removes it without changing what binds (the generator emits no SYSLIB1100/1101 diagnostics under TreatWarningsAsErrors, and McpAgent.Tests is unchanged from the P0.1 baseline: the same 8 failures, owned by BUG-BASELINE-002 and BUG-BASELINE-011); the full trim theory passes 8/8; accountability through TR-MCP-QUALITY-001 rather than a new TR is correct.\\nB7. BUG-BUILD-007 root cause: the receipt bug-build-007-evidence.log.txt shows the Build.Tests process blocked on EOF of an exited dotnet child while an MSBuild worker node (/nodemode:1 /nodeReuse:true) spawned by that child's build held both pipes as its stdout and stderr. Judge whether the evidence supports this and whether it explains the intermittency (the build only spawns a node when no idle reusable node exists).\\nB8. BUG-BUILD-007 fix: BoundedProcess (tests/Build.Tests/BoundedProcess.cs) bounds the exit wait and kills the process tree on timeout or cancellation; drains stdout and stderr concurrently; after the child exits, bounds the wait for the output to close and fails with IOException carrying the captured output; gives dotnet children --disable-build-servers; and has no race, leak, or deadlock that matters in a test process (abandoned pumps on a held pipe, Process.Dispose semantics for StandardOutput in sync read mode, CancellationTokenSource disposal after cancel, sync-over-async in Run). All six former call sites use it with sensible timeouts, and the AC-006 source guard would catch a new direct read or wait. Assess the Windows behavior of the AC-001 test (a pwsh child started with Start-Process -NoNewWindow must inherit the redirected handles on Windows as it does on Linux) and of --disable-build-servers on windows-latest; mark UNKNOWN rather than PASS where you cannot verify Windows behavior.\\nB9. BUG-BUILD-009: TryDeleteArtifacts deleted only through a detached cmd.exe, so on Linux and macOS (no cmd.exe) the Win32Exception was swallowed and every trim run leaked eight artifact trees; the fix deletes in place off Windows and keeps the non-blocking Windows path; TrimArtifactCleanupTests would catch a regression on every OS.\\nB10. Test-first order (Byrd v4): for each bug a RED run failed on an assertion before the fix and the same test passes after it; the receipts show both runs (for BUG-BUILD-004 and BUG-BUILD-006 the RED is the pre-existing failing case in the full Build.Tests run recorded in the P0.1 receipts).\\nB11. Gates: the targeted tests pass with zero skips; the full Build.Tests run in the default environment (node reuse not disabled) completes without a hang, and its only failures are the two BUG-BUILD-008 checksum cases; ./build.ps1 Compile and ./build.ps1 ValidateConfig succeed. Every remaining failure predates these changes, is filed in triage, and is tracked under its own TODO (verify ids).\\nB12. Requirements: TR-MCP-NUKE-002, -006, -007, -008, -009, -010 exist in the live store under FR-MCP-BUILD-001 with acceptance criteria that match the change and the tests named as evidence; none has a TEST record (operator ruling); BUG-BUILD-006 is correctly accountable through TR-MCP-QUALITY-001.\\nB13. Conventions: XML docs on every new member and test (TreatWarningsAsErrors and GenerateDocumentationFile are global); new files carry the Apache-2.0 SPDX header; existing files keep their license state; no package versions outside Directory.Packages.props; each commit carries the signature line and Co-Authored-By trailer.\\nB14. Records parity: commit messages, receipts, TODO implementationTasks for BUG-BUILD-001..007 and -009, triage reports, requirements, and the implementer's session-log records state only what the evidence shows, with nothing claimed done that is not.\\n\\nFor every FAIL give: the location (file and line, or record id), the exact defect, evidence, and the specific change that would make it PASS. State whether the fix is an implementer edit or needs an operator decision (name the decision and the options).\\n\\nRECEIPTS (mandatory): docs/receipts/hv/hostile-validator-bug-build-001-009-{UTC}.md and .json (native PowerShell objects, ConvertTo-Json); the runner writes request/response JSONL (paths below); your MCP reviewer turn holds the ENTIRE result with persistence proof. Include TimestampUtc, ValidatorIdentity with live proof, add-profile count, marker and memory read confirmation, each claim PASS|FAIL|UNKNOWN with evidence, the commands you ran and their exit codes, OverallVerdict, Accuracy, Completeness, Confidence, FAIL and UNKNOWN lists, implementer-fix vs operator-decision classification, reviewer sessionId/requestId. Prefer PowerShell. No Python. One round only.\\nEnd with \\\"=== VERDICT JSON ===\\\" and one JSON object: overallVerdict, accuracy, completeness, confidence, passCount, failCount, unknownCount, failList, unknownList, implementerFixes, operatorDecisionFails, headSha, receiptPaths, reviewerSessionId, reviewerRequestId.\\n\\n{UTC} stamp for your receipt file names: 20261010T225520Z Request JSONL (written by the runner): /home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/session-20261009/docs/receipts/hv/20261010T225520Z-bug-build-001-009.request.jsonl Response JSONL (your --json stream, written by the runner): /home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/session-20261009/docs/receipts/hv/20261010T225520Z-bug-build-001-009.response.jsonl HEAD at launch: e0cb480e9b1ba3b46c74a6ac7b10d13e82be9a24\\n\"}\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
