{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command 'git status --short; git rev-parse HEAD; git log --oneline -15; git log --format=\\\"%h %s%n%b\\\" a90e8b4c\"'^..HEAD -- .nuke build tests/Build.Tests src/QBrainAi.McpAgent docs/receipts | Select-Object -First 160'\"' \"","aggregated_output":"?? docs/receipts/hv/20261010T225520Z-bug-build-001-009.request.jsonl\n?? docs/receipts/hv/20261010T225520Z-bug-build-001-009.response.jsonl\ne0cb480e9b1ba3b46c74a6ac7b10d13e82be9a24\ne0cb480e Record G1 after the BUG-BUILD-003..009 fixes\nc34d10c4 Record the BUG-BUILD-003..009 receipts\n704d5a34 Delete the trim-analysis artifacts off Windows too (BUG-BUILD-009)\n7d0c299e Bound every Build.Tests child process (BUG-BUILD-007)\n22da826a Bind McpAgent options through the source generator (BUG-BUILD-006)\n47b41d0d Let ValidateConfig read the QBrainAi config root (BUG-BUILD-005)\nd6cf2bfd Fix the stale InstallReplTool test sample (BUG-BUILD-004)\ncb8624f7 Resolve the plugin parent from .claude/worktrees (BUG-BUILD-003)\nc0356d27 Record the P0.1 toolchain gate and baselines\n8a8c73eb Map the plan's Nuke TRs to the build-tooling FR (amendment v4)\nfd8ad3a0 Amend PLAN-SESSIONTURNREVIEW-001 for the Build.Tests, Nuke, and lockfile rulings\na31cc4ff Classify Build.Tests as infrastructure, not unit tests, in CLAUDE.md\nc0f82356 Restore every project the Nuke Compile target builds (BUG-BUILD-002)\na90e8b4c Point the Nuke Solution parameter at QBrainAi.sln (BUG-BUILD-001)\n3fdb4b7b Pin dotnet-ef 10.0.0 as a repo local tool (P0.1)\ne0cb480e Record G1 after the BUG-BUILD-003..009 fixes\nAt c34d10c4, ./build.ps1 Compile succeeded (Restore 0:17, Compile\n2:40, 0 warnings, 0 errors), and ./build.ps1 ValidateConfig passed for\n2 instances. The logs are added to\ndocs/receipts/_bug-build-003-009-20261010T224959Z/ (worktree path made\nrelative, API keys redacted, 0 found), with a gate line in the\nsummary.\n\nSigned: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 99%, accuracy 99%, completeness 98%\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nc34d10c4 Record the BUG-BUILD-003..009 receipts\nRED, green, and gate logs for BUG-BUILD-003 (cb8624f7), -004\n(d6cf2bfd), -005 (47b41d0d), -006 (22da826a), -007 (7d0c299e), and\n-009 (704d5a34), including the live BUG-BUILD-007 root-cause\nsnapshot and both full Build.Tests runs, with the worktree path made\nrelative and API keys redacted (0 found). Summary:\ndocs/receipts/bug-build-003-009-20261010T224959Z.md.\n\nSigned: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 98%, accuracy 98%, completeness 97%\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n704d5a34 Delete the trim-analysis artifacts off Windows too (BUG-BUILD-009)\nTrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests.TryDeleteArtifacts (added in\n55fae924) removed a target's artifacts root only by starting a\ndetached cmd.exe /c rmdir, so that an antivirus scan on Windows cannot\nblock the test host. Linux and macOS have no cmd.exe: Process.Start\nthrew Win32Exception, the catch swallowed it, and every run of the\ntrim-inventory theory leaked eight artifact trees under\n<temp>/mcpserver-trim-analysis. By 2026-10-10 LAB-OMARCHY held 38\nrun directories, 4.0 GB, in a tmpfs /tmp. Off Windows the cleanup now\ndeletes in place. Windows keeps its non-blocking path. The method is\ninternal so TrimArtifactCleanupTests can call it.\n\nAccountability: TR-MCP-NUKE-010, created under FR-MCP-BUILD-001\n\"Tooling for repeatable builds\".\nTriage: triage-report-410efece19aa4877931d88b4aa9f0928.\nThe directories already leaked (46, 5.0 GB, after the BUG-BUILD-007\ngate run) are left for the operator.\n\nByrd v4:\n- RED: TrimArtifactCleanupTests.TryDeleteArtifacts_PopulatedRoot_IsRemoved\n  failed after its 30 s poll (\"TryDeleteArtifacts left ... in\n  place\"; Failed 1, Passed 0, Skipped 0).\n- Green: the same test passes (Passed 1, Skipped 0, 38 ms).\n- Gate: the full Build.Tests suite (Failed 2, Passed 363, Skipped 0;\n  the two failures are the BUG-BUILD-008 checksum cases) left no new\n  directory under mcpserver-trim-analysis (46 before, 46 after).\n\nSigned: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 97%, accuracy 98%, completeness 96%\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n7d0c299e Bound every Build.Tests child process (BUG-BUILD-007)\nThe Build.Tests infrastructure suite could hang because six helpers\nwaited for a child's redirected output with no bound. Root cause,\nobserved live on 2026-10-10 (Linux, SDK 10.0.201): the test process\n(0 s CPU, no children) was blocked on EOF of a dotnet child that had\nalready exited. An MSBuild worker node that the child's build had\nspawned (MSBuild.dll /nodemode:1 /nodeReuse:true, reparented to the\nuser systemd) held both pipes as its stdout and stderr. Node reuse\nkeeps such a node alive after the build, so EOF never arrives. When\nan idle reusable node already exists, the build connects to it and\nnothing inherits the pipes, which is why the suite sometimes passed.\n\nBoundedProcess is now the one way Build.Tests runs a child with\nredirected output. It bounds the wait for exit and kills the process\ntree on expiry or cancellation. It drains stdout and stderr\nconcurrently. After the child exits, it bounds the wait for the\noutput to close and fails fast with the captured output if a\ndescendant still holds it. It starts dotnet children with\n--disable-build-servers.\n\nAll six call sites use it:\n- MigrationAssemblyObsoleteWarningTests (dotnet build).\n- TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests (dotnet build and publish; its\n  20-minute timeout bounded only the exit, not the output).\n- RequirementsWikiPublishScriptTests (pwsh; it read stdout to the\n  end before stderr, which could also deadlock on a full stderr pipe).\n- YamlObjectMutationTests (pwsh).\n- Both ServiceUpdateTests process runners (exit bounded at 30 s,\n  then an unbounded Task.WaitAll).\n\nAccountability: TR-MCP-NUKE-009 (AC-001..AC-006), created under\nFR-MCP-BUILD-001 \"Tooling for repeatable builds\".\nTriage: triage-report-c381e4c99d284e0dbc1ec443c221ca59.\n\nByrd v4:\n- RED: BoundedProcessTests against a stub with the unbounded\n  pattern: Failed 5, Passed 1, Skipped 0, all on assertions.\n  - The held-output case waited 30 s for the descendant (\"No\n    exception was thrown\"), and the timeout case waited 60 s.\n  - The cancelled child outlived the cancellation.\n  - --disable-build-servers was missing.\n  - The source guard listed the six call sites (16 lines).\n  - The concurrent-drain case passed on the stub and stays as a\n    characterization test.\n- Green: the first run failed only the source guard. It flagged\n  result.StandardOutput because the result record shared the Process\n  property names, so the record now uses Stdout and Stderr and the\n  guard stays broad. BoundedProcessTests then passed (Passed 6,\n  Failed 0, Skipped 0).\n- Gate: the full Build.Tests suite in the default environment (node\n  reuse not disabled) completed in 4 m 20 s: Failed 2, Passed 362,\n  Skipped 0. The two failures are the BUG-BUILD-008 checksum cases.\n  No MSBuild worker node was left running.\n\nSigned: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 96%, accuracy 98%, completeness 96%\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n22da826a Bind McpAgent options through the source generator (BUG-BUILD-006)\n789a9e91 (\"Keep 1.x route, config, schema, and install aliases.\",\n2026-10-05) made AddQBrainAiMcpAgent bind McpAgentOptions with\nconfiguration.GetSection(sectionName).Bind(options)\n(ServiceCollectionExtensions.cs:49). ConfigurationBinder.Bind\n(IConfiguration, Object) is reflection-based and carries\nRequiresUnreferencedCode, so with the repository's trim-warning\nsuppression disabled the analyzer reports IL2026 there, and\nTrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests found IL2026 = 2 against the empty\ncaptured inventory of QBrainAi.McpAgent. The library is packable and\nits inventory stays empty, so the fix is in the code, not the\ninventory: EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator makes the compiler\nintercept the Bind call with generated, trim-safe binding code.\n\nAccountability: TR-MCP-QUALITY-001 (an unapproved warning stays open\nremediation work until fixed and validated), checked by the W19\ntrim inventory (TEST-MCP-AIUNIT-002).\nTriage: triage-report-dbbbec24a03a4d70856cfe9c5fd7ab80.\n\nByrd v4:\n- RED: TrimAnalysis_WithRepositorySuppressionDisabled_MatchesCapturedInventory\n  (target: QBrainAi.McpAgent) failed with \"Dictionaries differ\"\n  (Expected [], Actual [IL2026 = 2]).\n- Green: the full trim theory passes (Passed 8, Failed 0, Skipped 0).\n  It ran with MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1, so the BUG-BUILD-007 pipe\n  hang could not stall it. dotnet build of the project reports\n  0 warnings. QBrainAi.McpAgent.Tests matches the P0.1 baseline: the\n  same 8 failures with identical messages, owned by BUG-BASELINE-002\n  and BUG-BASELINE-011 (Passed 57, Skipped 0).\n\nSigned: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 97%, accuracy 98%, completeness 95%\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n47b41d0d Let ValidateConfig read the QBrainAi config root (BUG-BUILD-005)\nAfter the QBrainAi rename, the live appsettings.yaml root is QBrainAi:\n(line 46), but ConfigValidator matched only ^Mcp:, so ParseInstances\nreturned null and ./build.ps1 ValidateConfig threw \"Missing Mcp\nsection in config.\", which failed G5. The server reads both roots\nthrough CanonicalSectionProjectionProvider. The validator now accepts\nthe canonical QBrainAi: root and the legacy Mcp: root, and the error\nnames both.\n\nAccountability: TR-MCP-NUKE-008, created under FR-MCP-BUILD-001\n\"Tooling for repeatable builds\".\nTriage: triage-report-dbbbec24a03a4d70856cfe9c5fd7ab80.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
