j | 2 ++\n 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)\n7d0c299e Bound every Build.Tests child process (BUG-BUILD-007)\n tests/Build.Tests/BoundedProcess.cs                | 186 +++++++++++++++++\n tests/Build.Tests/BoundedProcessTests.cs           | 223 +++++++++++++++++++++\n .../MigrationAssemblyObsoleteWarningTests.cs       |  27 +--\n .../RequirementsWikiPublishScriptTests.cs          |   7 +-\n tests/Build.Tests/ServiceUpdateTests.cs            |  20 +-\n .../TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests.cs           |  39 +---\n tests/Build.Tests/YamlObjectMutationTests.cs       |  27 +--\n 7 files changed, 438 insertions(+), 91 deletions(-)\n704d5a34 Delete the trim-analysis artifacts off Windows too (BUG-BUILD-009)\n .../TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests.cs           | 23 ++++++++++--\n tests/Build.Tests/TrimArtifactCleanupTests.cs      | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 63 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\ncommit a90e8b4c27f9a56c2a994abc276012f76a743c50\nAuthor:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nAuthorDate: Sat Oct 10 11:43:59 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nCommitDate: Sat Oct 10 11:43:59 2026 -0500\n\n    Point the Nuke Solution parameter at QBrainAi.sln (BUG-BUILD-001)\n    \n    .nuke/parameters.json still named McpServer.sln, which the QBrainAi\n    rename removed. Nuke could not inject Build.Solution, so Restore threw\n    NullReferenceException, and every ./build.ps1 target that depends on it\n    failed before running a test. P0.1 of PLAN-SESSIONTURNREVIEW-001 found\n    this on the approval HEAD; origin/develop has the same parameters file.\n    Triage: triage-report-5b07fc9222b543b0810889bc9fcc31e2.\n    \n    Byrd v4:\n    - RED: NukeParametersTests.NukeParameters_Solution_NamesExistingSolutionFile\n      failed with \"names Solution 'McpServer.sln', which does not exist\"\n      (Failed 1, Passed 0, Skipped 0).\n    - Fix: Solution = QBrainAi.sln.\n    - Green: the test passes (Passed 1, Skipped 0), and ./build.ps1 Compile\n      now runs Restore successfully.\n    \n    Two follow-ups remain, both older than this change and filed separately:\n    - Compile still fails on a project outside the solution.\n    - The full Build.Tests run shows 5 failures that do not read this file.\n    \n    Nuke regenerated .nuke/build.schema.json on these runs. The committed\n    copy still had pre-rename descriptions; only description strings change.\n    The new test file carries the Apache-2.0 SPDX header.\n    \n    Signed: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 97%, accuracy 97%, completeness 95%\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ncommit c0f823565e53bbc6075d7451e3f82004a1805a1e\nAuthor:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nAuthorDate: Sat Oct 10 13:36:24 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nCommitDate: Sat Oct 10 13:36:24 2026 -0500\n\n    Restore every project the Nuke Compile target builds (BUG-BUILD-002)\n    \n    Compile built every *.csproj under src/ and tests/ (except Build.Tests)\n    with --no-restore, but Restore restored only QBrainAi.sln. The seven\n    src/Compatibility/SharpNinja.McpServer.* 1.x alias projects are not in\n    the solution, so Compile failed with NETSDK1004 and ./build.ps1 Test\n    could not run. Triage: triage-report-fed753f7ec23496893a8bae0de0fefcc.\n    \n    Fix: Build.GetBuildProjectFiles holds the shared project set. Compile\n    builds it. Restore restores the solution, then each project of the set\n    that the solution does not list, compared by full path.\n    \n    Accountability: TR-MCP-NUKE-002, created in the requirements store\n    with no FR mapping (operator ruling 2026-10-10: \"NUKE is only\n    accountable through TR.\"). NukeParametersTests (BUG-BUILD-001) and the\n    new tests cite it instead of the old TEST-NUKE-001 label. Build.Tests\n    is the infrastructure suite, not unit tests (operator ruling, same day).\n    \n    Byrd v4:\n    - RED: BuildProjectSetTests failed on assertions against an empty\n      GetBuildProjectFiles stub (Failed 2, Passed 0, Skipped 0).\n    - A read-only reviewer found that BuildTargetTests.cs:431-432 pinned\n      the old inline enumeration text. The next full Build.Tests run\n      showed that case failing; its two assertions now name the helper's\n      text.\n    - Green: the targeted cases pass (Passed 4, Skipped 0).\n    - ./build.ps1 Test: Restore and Compile succeed. Restore restores the\n      solution plus exactly the seven Compatibility projects, and all 53\n      build projects compile. The Test target then stops on pre-existing\n      unit failures, which are filed separately.\n    - Full Build.Tests: 346 of 354 tests ran (Failed 5, Passed 341, Skipped 0). All five failures are pre-existing infrastructure defects tracked as BUG-BUILD-003..006. The run then stalled in MigrationAssemblies_CompileSuccessfully, and --blame-hang killed it after 10 minutes; that hang is filed as BUG-BUILD-007 (triage-report-c381e4c99d284e0dbc1ec443c221ca59).\n    \n    Signed: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 96%, accuracy 96%, completeness 94%\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ncommit cb8624f7b4ba7ebacea3c362f98a29fd2f14c41e\nAuthor:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nAuthorDate: Sat Oct 10 16:56:59 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nCommitDate: Sat Oct 10 16:56:59 2026 -0500\n\n    Resolve the plugin parent from .claude/worktrees (BUG-BUILD-003)\n    \n    Build.ResolveOfficialPluginSiblingParent walked up from a worktree and,\n    on reaching a \"worktrees\" folder, stepped past only a .mcpServer parent.\n    From .claude/worktrees/<name> (Claude Code worktrees) it returned the\n    McpServer checkout instead of its parent, so SyncAgentPlugins defaults\n    and the plugin-core checksum tests found no plugin repos (\"plugin root\n    missing\"). It now steps past any dot-folder of the checkout.\n    \n    Accountability: TR-MCP-NUKE-006 (created in the requirements store\n    under FR-MCP-BUILD-001 \"Tooling for repeatable builds\"; operator,\n    2026-10-10: \"Now, the TR are implementation detail of the FR.\").\n    Triage: triage-report-75290be6d6b749119a7819fba3cca386.\n    \n    Byrd v4:\n    - RED: PluginParentResolutionTests (new, SPDX Apache-2.0) failed only\n      for the .claude/worktrees layout, returning \".../McpServer\" (Failed 1,\n      Passed 2, Skipped 0).\n    - Green: all three layouts pass.\n    \n    The checksum tests now find all five official plugins. They report a\n    separate, pre-existing problem: 19 lib-ps files drift from the canonical\n    plugins/core/lib-ps. The plugins were last synced 2026-10-01 or\n    2026-09-19, and the canonical core changed 2026-10-05. That is filed\n    separately, because fixing it means running SyncAgentPlugins.\n    \n    Signed: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 97%, accuracy 97%, completeness 95%\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ncommit d6cf2bfd0c60ff9343bfa7ad5547c11c2b9c78ae\nAuthor:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nAuthorDate: Sat Oct 10 16:59:16 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nCommitDate: Sat Oct 10 16:59:16 2026 -0500\n\n    Fix the stale InstallReplTool test sample (BUG-BUILD-004)\n    \n    The rename commit 6de989f3 changed the test samples command to\n    qbrain-ai-repl and the lookup id to QBrainAI.Repl but left the package\n    id column at sharpninja.mcpserver.repl, so the lookup found nothing.\n    The code is correct: InstallReplTool installs QBrainAI.Repl and looks it\n    up by id. The 1.x alias SharpNinja.McpServer.Repl (mcpserver-repl,\n    TR-MCP-QBRAIN-003) is a different tool; dotnet tool list --global on\n    this host shows exactly that alias installed.\n    \n    The sample now lists qbrainai.repl, which is how dotnet prints the id,\n    next to the alias. The test asserts that each lookup returns only its\n    own packages version.\n    \n    Accountability: TR-MCP-NUKE-007, created under FR-MCP-BUILD-001\n    \"Tooling for repeatable builds\". RED: the existing case failed with\n    Expected \"6.1.1\", Actual null in every Build.Tests run today. Green:\n    Passed 1, Skipped 0. No code change.\n    Triage: triage-report-dbbbec24a03a4d70856cfe9c5fd7ab80.\n    \n    Signed: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 98%, accuracy 98%, completeness 96%\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ncommit 47b41d0d0e76bf8b6893dd46fb81583f1ddbbfe4\nAuthor:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nAuthorDate: Sat Oct 10 17:01:09 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nCommitDate: Sat Oct 10 17:01:09 2026 -0500\n\n    Let ValidateConfig read the QBrainAi config root (BUG-BUILD-005)\n    \n    After the QBrainAi rename, the live appsettings.yaml root is QBrainAi:\n    (line 46), but ConfigValidator matched only ^Mcp:, so ParseInstances\n    returned null and ./build.ps1 ValidateConfig threw \"Missing Mcp\n    section in config.\", which failed G5. The server reads both roots\n    through CanonicalSectionProjectionProvider. The validator now accepts\n    the canonical QBrainAi: root and the legacy Mcp: root, and the error\n    names both.\n    \n    Accountability: TR-MCP-NUKE-008, created under FR-MCP-BUILD-001\n    \"Tooling for repeatable builds\".\n    Triage: triage-report-dbbbec24a03a4d70856cfe9c5fd7ab80.\n    \n    Byrd v4:\n    - RED: ConfigValidatorTests.ParseInstances_QBrainAiRoot_ReturnsInstances\n      (new) and G8_ValidateConfig_ShippedValidator_PassesOnLiveAppsettings\n      both failed with Assert.NotNull (Failed 2, Passed 0, Skipped 0).\n    - Green: ConfigValidatorTests and the G8 case pass (Passed 14,\n      Skipped 0), and ./build.ps1 ValidateConfig succeeds (\"MCP config\n      validation passed for 2 instances\").\n    \n    Signed: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 98%, accuracy 98%, completeness 96%\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ncommit 22da826ab53fb673e0483215ba005a02559d6514\nAuthor:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nAuthorDate: Sat Oct 10 17:27:09 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nCommitDate: Sat Oct 10 17:27:09 2026 -0500\n\n    Bind McpAgent options through the source generator (BUG-BUILD-006)\n    \n    789a9e91 (\"Keep 1.x route, config, schema, and install aliases.\",\n    2026-10-05) made AddQBrainAiMcpAgent bind McpAgentOptions with\n    configuration.GetSection(sectionName).Bind(options)\n    (ServiceCollectionExtensions.cs:49). ConfigurationBinder.Bind\n    (IConfiguration, Object) is reflection-based and carries\n    RequiresUnreferencedCode, so with the repository's trim-warning\n    suppression disabled the analyzer reports IL2026 there, and\n    TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests found IL2026 = 2 against the empty\n    captured inventory of QBrainAi.McpAgent. The library is packable and\n    its inventory stays empty, so the fix is in the code, not the\n    inventory: EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator makes the compiler\n    intercept the Bind call with generated, trim-safe binding code.\n    \n    Accountability: TR-MCP-QUALITY-001 (an unapproved warning stays open\n    remediation work until fixed and validated), checked by the W19\n    trim inventory (TEST-MCP-AIUNIT-002).\n    Triage: triage-report-dbbbec24a03a4d70856cfe9c5fd7ab80.\n    \n    Byrd v4:\n    - RED: TrimAnalysis_WithRepositorySuppressionDisabled_MatchesCapturedInventory\n      (target: QBrainAi.McpAgent) failed with \"Dictionaries differ\"\n      (Expected [], Actual [IL2026 = 2]).\n    - Green: the full trim theory passes (Passed 8, Failed 0, Skipped 0).\n      It ran with MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1, so the BUG-BUILD-007 pipe\n      hang could not stall it. dotnet build of the project reports\n      0 warnings. QBrainAi.McpAgent.Tests matches the P0.1 baseline: the\n      same 8 failures with identical messages, owned by BUG-BASELINE-002\n      and BUG-BASELINE-011 (Passed 57, Skipped 0).\n    \n    Signed: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 97%, accuracy 98%, completeness 95%\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ncommit 7d0c299ef32e93bc672d107b1ec2008502ed9519\nAuthor:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nAuthorDate: Sat Oct 10 17:42:55 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nCommitDate: Sat Oct 10 17:42:55 2026 -0500\n\n    Bound every Build.Tests child process (BUG-BUILD-007)\n    \n    The Build.Tests infrastructure suite could hang because six helpers\n    waited for a child's redirected output with no bound. Root cause,\n    observed live on 2026-10-10 (Linux, SDK 10.0.201): the test process\n    (0 s CPU, no children) was blocked on EOF of a dotnet child that had\n    already exited. An MSBuild worker node that the child's build had\n    spawned (MSBuild.dll /nodemode:1 /nodeReuse:true, reparented to the\n    user systemd) held both pipes as its stdout and stderr. Node reuse\n    keeps such a node alive after the build, so EOF never arrives. When\n    an idle reusable node already exists, the build connects to it and\n    nothing inherits the pipes, which is why the suite sometimes passed.\n    \n    BoundedProcess is now the one way Build.Tests runs a child with\n    redirected output. It bounds the wait for exit and kills the process\n    tree on expiry or cancellation. It drains stdout and stderr\n    concurrently. After the child exits, it bounds the wait for the\n    output to close and fails fast with the captured output if a\n    descendant still holds it. It starts dotnet children with\n    --disable-build-servers.\n    \n    All six call sites use it:\n    - MigrationAssemblyObsoleteWarningTests (dotnet build).\n    - TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests (dotnet build and publish; its\n      20-minute timeout bounded only the exit, not the output).\n    - RequirementsWikiPublishScriptTests (pwsh; it read stdout to the\n      end before stderr, which could also deadlock on a full stderr pipe).\n    - YamlObjectMutationTests (pwsh).\n    - Both ServiceUpdateTests process runners (exit bounded at 30 s,\n      then an unbounded Task.WaitAll).\n    \n    Accountability: TR-MCP-NUKE-009 (AC-001..AC-006), created under\n    FR-MCP-BUILD-001 \"Tooling for repeatable builds\".\n    Triage: triage-report-c381e4c99d284e0dbc1ec443c221ca59.\n    \n    Byrd v4:\n    - RED: BoundedProcessTests against a stub with the unbounded\n      pattern: Failed 5, Passed 1, Skipped 0, all on assertions.\n      - The held-output case waited 30 s for the descendant (\"No\n        exception was thrown\"), and the timeout case waited 60 s.\n      - The cancelled child outlived the cancellation.\n      - --disable-build-servers was missing.\n      - The source guard listed the six call sites (16 lines).\n      - The concurrent-drain case passed on the stub and stays as a\n        characterization test.\n    - Green: the first run failed only the source guard. It flagged\n      result.StandardOutput because the result record shared the Process\n      property names, so the record now uses Stdout and Stderr and the\n      guard stays broad. BoundedProcessTests then passed (Passed 6,\n      Failed 0, Skipped 0).\n    - Gate: the full Build.Tests suite in the default environment (node\n      reuse not disabled) completed in 4 m 20 s: Failed 2, Passed 362,\n      Skipped 0. The two failures are the BUG-BUILD-008 checksum cases.\n      No MSBuild worker node was left running.\n    \n    Signed: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 96%, accuracy 98%, completeness 96%\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ncommit 704d5a34ae4b315f0c89c743dd837ac97865dbe8\nAuthor:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nAuthorDate: Sat Oct 10 17:49:38 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Sharp Ninja <ninja@thesharp.ninja>\nCommitDate: Sat Oct 10 17:49:38 2026 -0500\n\n    Delete the trim-analysis artifacts off Windows too (BUG-BUILD-009)\n    \n    TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests.TryDeleteArtifacts (added in\n    55fae924) removed a target's artifacts root only by starting a\n    detached cmd.exe /c rmdir, so that an antivirus scan on Windows cannot\n    block the test host. Linux and macOS have no cmd.exe: Process.Start\n    threw Win32Exception, the catch swallowed it, and every run of the\n    trim-inventory theory leaked eight artifact trees under\n    <temp>/mcpserver-trim-analysis. By 2026-10-10 LAB-OMARCHY held 38\n    run directories, 4.0 GB, in a tmpfs /tmp. Off Windows the cleanup now\n    deletes in place. Windows keeps its non-blocking path. The method is\n    internal so TrimArtifactCleanupTests can call it.\n    \n    Accountability: TR-MCP-NUKE-010, created under FR-MCP-BUILD-001\n    \"Tooling for repeatable builds\".\n    Triage: triage-report-410efece19aa4877931d88b4aa9f0928.\n    The directories already leaked (46, 5.0 GB, after the BUG-BUILD-007\n    gate run) are left for the operator.\n    \n    Byrd v4:\n    - RED: TrimArtifactCleanupTests.TryDeleteArtifacts_PopulatedRoot_IsRemoved\n      failed after its 30 s poll (\"TryDeleteArtifacts left ... in\n      place\"; Failed 1, Passed 0, Skipped 0).\n    - Green: the same test passes (Passed 1, Skipped 0, 38 ms).\n    - Gate: the full Build.Tests suite (Failed 2, Passed 363, Skipped 0;\n      the two failures are the BUG-BUILD-008 checksum cases) left no new\n      directory under mcpserver-trim-analysis (46 before, 46 after).\n    \n    Signed: claude-opus-5-5-max@ClaudeCode | Confidence: correctness 97%, accuracy 98%, completeness 96%\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command 'Get-Content tests/Build.Tests/BoundedProcess.cs; Get-Content tests/Build.Tests/BoundedProcessTests.cs; Get-Content tests/Build.Tests/TrimArtifactCleanupTests.cs' \"","aggregated_output":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\nusing System.Diagnostics;\nusing System.Text;\n\nnamespace NukeBuild.Tests;\n\n/// <summary>\n/// TR-MCP-NUKE-009 (BUG-BUILD-007): the one way the Build.Tests infrastructure suite runs a child process with redirected output.\n/// It bounds the wait for the child to exit and, once the child has exited, the wait for its output to close; drains standard\n/// output and standard error concurrently; kills the child's process tree on timeout or cancellation; and starts dotnet children\n/// with <c>--disable-build-servers</c>. Without these bounds a descendant that inherits the child's pipes, such as an MSBuild worker\n/// node started with node reuse, holds them open after the child exits, and the suite waits for an end of stream that never comes.\n/// </summary>\ninternal static class BoundedProcess\n{\n    private const int CapturedTailLength = 4000;\n\n    /// <summary>TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-001: how long to wait for redirected output to close after the child exits.</summary>\n    internal static readonly TimeSpan DefaultDrainTimeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30);\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-005: a <c>dotnet</c> start info for <paramref name=\"arguments\"/> that ignores persistent build servers, so\n    /// no MSBuild worker node, MSBuild server, or compiler server outlives the child holding its redirected output.\n    /// </summary>\n    internal static ProcessStartInfo Dotnet(string workingDirectory, IEnumerable<string> arguments)\n    {\n        var startInfo = new ProcessStartInfo(\"dotnet\") { WorkingDirectory = workingDirectory };\n        foreach (var argument in arguments)\n        {\n            startInfo.ArgumentList.Add(argument);\n        }\n\n        startInfo.ArgumentList.Add(\"--disable-build-servers\");\n        return startInfo;\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>Synchronous <see cref=\"RunAsync(ProcessStartInfo, TimeSpan, CancellationToken)\"/> for synchronous fixtures.</summary>\n    internal static BoundedProcessResult Run(ProcessStartInfo startInfo, TimeSpan exitTimeout, CancellationToken cancellationToken) =>\n        RunAsync(startInfo, exitTimeout, DefaultDrainTimeout, cancellationToken).GetAwaiter().GetResult();\n\n    /// <summary>Runs the child with the default drain period, <see cref=\"DefaultDrainTimeout\"/>.</summary>\n    internal static Task<BoundedProcessResult> RunAsync(ProcessStartInfo startInfo, TimeSpan exitTimeout, CancellationToken cancellationToken) =>\n        RunAsync(startInfo, exitTimeout, DefaultDrainTimeout, cancellationToken);\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-001..AC-004: starts the child with redirected output, drains standard output and standard error\n    /// concurrently, and returns the exit code with the complete output.\n    /// </summary>\n    /// <exception cref=\"TimeoutException\">The child ran past <paramref name=\"exitTimeout\"/>; its process tree was killed.</exception>\n    /// <exception cref=\"OperationCanceledException\">The caller cancelled; a still-running child's process tree was killed.</exception>\n    /// <exception cref=\"IOException\">The child exited, but its output was still open <paramref name=\"drainTimeout\"/> later.</exception>\n    internal static async Task<BoundedProcessResult> RunAsync(\n        ProcessStartInfo startInfo,\n        TimeSpan exitTimeout,\n        TimeSpan drainTimeout,\n        CancellationToken cancellationToken)\n    {\n        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(startInfo);\n        startInfo.UseShellExecute = false;\n        startInfo.RedirectStandardOutput = true;\n        startInfo.RedirectStandardError = true;\n        var command = Describe(startInfo);\n        var stdout = new StringBuilder();\n        var stderr = new StringBuilder();\n        using var abandon = new CancellationTokenSource();\n        using var process = Process.Start(startInfo) ?? throw new InvalidOperationException($\"Failed to start {command}.\");\n        var output = Task.WhenAll(\n            PumpAsync(process.StandardOutput, stdout, abandon.Token),\n            PumpAsync(process.StandardError, stderr, abandon.Token));\n\n        using (var exit = CancellationTokenSource.CreateLinkedTokenSource(cancellationToken))\n        {\n            exit.CancelAfter(exitTimeout);\n            try\n            {\n                await process.WaitForExitAsync(exit.Token).ConfigureAwait(false);\n            }\n            catch (OperationCanceledException)\n            {\n                await KillTreeAsync(process).ConfigureAwait(false);\n                await abandon.CancelAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);\n                cancellationToken.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();\n                throw new TimeoutException(\n                    $\"{command} did not exit within {exitTimeout}; its process tree was killed.{Captured(stdout, stderr)}\");\n            }\n        }\n\n        // AC-001: the child has exited, but its output closes only when every holder of the pipes' write ends has closed them.\n        try\n        {\n            await output.WaitAsync(drainTimeout, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n        }\n        catch (TimeoutException)\n        {\n            await abandon.CancelAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);\n            throw new IOException(\n                $\"{command} exited with code {process.ExitCode}, but its redirected output was still open {drainTimeout} later: a \"\n                + $\"descendant process inherited the pipes, so the captured output may be incomplete.{Captured(stdout, stderr)}\");\n        }\n        catch (OperationCanceledException)\n        {\n            await abandon.CancelAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);\n            throw;\n        }\n\n        return new BoundedProcessResult(process.ExitCode, Snapshot(stdout), Snapshot(stderr));\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// Copies one redirected stream into <paramref name=\"sink\"/> until it closes. A read blocked on a pipe that a descendant holds\n    /// open cannot be interrupted, so an abandoned pump simply finishes whenever the last writer closes the pipe.\n    /// </summary>\n    private static async Task PumpAsync(StreamReader reader, StringBuilder sink, CancellationToken abandoned)\n    {\n        var buffer = new char[4096];\n        try\n        {\n            int read;\n            while ((read = await reader.ReadAsync(buffer.AsMemory(), abandoned).ConfigureAwait(false)) > 0)\n            {\n                lock (sink)\n                {\n                    sink.Append(buffer, 0, read);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        catch (Exception exception) when (abandoned.IsCancellationRequested\n            && exception is OperationCanceledException or ObjectDisposedException or IOException)\n        {\n            // Abandoned after a timeout, a cancellation, or output held open; what was read is already in the sink.\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-002, AC-003: kills the child and its descendants, then waits briefly for the kill to land.</summary>\n    private static async Task KillTreeAsync(Process process)\n    {\n        try\n        {\n            process.Kill(entireProcessTree: true);\n        }\n        catch (InvalidOperationException)\n        {\n            // The child exited between the timeout and the kill.\n        }\n\n        using var reaped = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(10));\n        try\n        {\n            await process.WaitForExitAsync(reaped.Token).ConfigureAwait(false);\n        }\n        catch (OperationCanceledException)\n        {\n            // Killed but not yet reaped; the caller still gets the timeout or the cancellation.\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static string Describe(ProcessStartInfo startInfo)\n    {\n        if (startInfo.ArgumentList.Count > 0)\n        {\n            return $\"{startInfo.FileName} {string.Join(' ', startInfo.ArgumentList)}\";\n        }\n\n        return string.IsNullOrEmpty(startInfo.Arguments) ? startInfo.FileName : $\"{startInfo.FileName} {startInfo.Arguments}\";\n    }\n\n    private static string Snapshot(StringBuilder sink)\n    {\n        lock (sink)\n        {\n            return sink.ToString();\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static string Captured(StringBuilder stdout, StringBuilder stderr) =>\n        $\"{Environment.NewLine}stdout:{Environment.NewLine}{Tail(Snapshot(stdout))}\"\n        + $\"{Environment.NewLine}stderr:{Environment.NewLine}{Tail(Snapshot(stderr))}\";\n\n    private static string Tail(string text) => text.Length <= CapturedTailLength ? text : \"...\" + text[^CapturedTailLength..];\n}\n\n/// <summary>TR-MCP-NUKE-009: a finished child's exit code and its complete redirected output.</summary>\n/// <param name=\"ExitCode\">The child's exit code.</param>\n/// <param name=\"Stdout\">Everything the child wrote to standard output.</param>\n/// <param name=\"Stderr\">Everything the child wrote to standard error.</param>\ninternal sealed record BoundedProcessResult(int ExitCode, string Stdout, string Stderr);\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\nusing System.Diagnostics;\n\nnamespace NukeBuild.Tests;\n\n/// <summary>\n/// TR-MCP-NUKE-009 (BUG-BUILD-007): verifies <see cref=\"BoundedProcess\"/>, the one way Build.Tests runs a child process with\n/// redirected output. Build-infrastructure test, accountable through TR only. The process cases start real <c>pwsh</c> children\n/// (no mocks); each writes the process id it must clean up to a temporary file that the test removes.\n/// </summary>\npublic sealed class BoundedProcessTests\n{\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-001: a child that exits while a descendant still holds its redirected output makes RunAsync fail within\n    /// the drain period, naming the command and keeping what the child wrote, instead of waiting for the descendant. The pwsh child\n    /// starts a second pwsh with <c>Start-Process -NoNewWindow</c>, which inherits the child's stdout and stderr as an MSBuild worker\n    /// node started with node reuse does (the BUG-BUILD-007 root cause), records its process id, and exits; the descendant sleeps 30 s.\n    /// </summary>\n    [Fact]\n    public async Task RunAsync_DescendantHoldsOutputAfterChildExits_FailsWithinDrainPeriod()\n    {\n        var pidFile = NewPidFile();\n        var command = \"$descendant = Start-Process -FilePath (Get-Process -Id $PID).Path -ArgumentList '-NoLogo','-NoProfile',\"\n            + \"'-NonInteractive','-Command','Start-Sleep -Seconds 30' -NoNewWindow -PassThru; \"\n            + $\"Set-Content -LiteralPath '{pidFile}' -Value $descendant.Id; 'child-exited'\";\n        var stopwatch = Stopwatch.StartNew();\n        try\n        {\n            var exception = await Assert.ThrowsAsync<IOException>(() => BoundedProcess.RunAsync(\n                Pwsh(command), TimeSpan.FromMinutes(1), TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2), TestContext.Current.CancellationToken));\n\n            Assert.True(stopwatch.Elapsed < TimeSpan.FromSeconds(20), $\"RunAsync waited {stopwatch.Elapsed} for the descendant.\");\n            Assert.Contains(\"pwsh\", exception.Message, StringComparison.Ordinal);\n            Assert.Contains(\"child-exited\", exception.Message, StringComparison.Ordinal);\n        }\n        finally\n        {\n            KillRecorded(pidFile);\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-002: a child that runs past its exit timeout is killed with its process tree and RunAsync throws a\n    /// <see cref=\"TimeoutException\"/> naming the command. The pwsh child records its own process id and sleeps 60 s; the exit\n    /// timeout is 10 s.\n    /// </summary>\n    [Fact]\n    public async Task RunAsync_ChildRunsPastExitTimeout_KillsTreeAndThrowsTimeout()\n    {\n        var pidFile = NewPidFile();\n        var command = $\"Set-Content -LiteralPath '{pidFile}' -Value $PID; Start-Sleep -Seconds 60\";\n        var stopwatch = Stopwatch.StartNew();\n        try\n        {\n            var exception = await Assert.ThrowsAsync<TimeoutException>(() => BoundedProcess.RunAsync(\n                Pwsh(command), TimeSpan.FromSeconds(10), TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2), TestContext.Current.CancellationToken));\n\n            Assert.True(stopwatch.Elapsed < TimeSpan.FromSeconds(40), $\"RunAsync returned after {stopwatch.Elapsed}.\");\n            Assert.Contains(\"pwsh\", exception.Message, StringComparison.Ordinal);\n            Assert.True(HasExited(pidFile), \"The child outlived its exit timeout.\");\n        }\n        finally\n        {\n            KillRecorded(pidFile);\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-003: when the caller cancels, RunAsync kills the child's process tree and stops waiting. The pwsh child\n    /// records its own process id and sleeps 60 s; the caller cancels after 10 s.\n    /// </summary>\n    [Fact]\n    public async Task RunAsync_CallerCancels_KillsTreeAndStopsWaiting()\n    {\n        var pidFile = NewPidFile();\n        var command = $\"Set-Content -LiteralPath '{pidFile}' -Value $PID; Start-Sleep -Seconds 60\";\n        using var cancellation = CancellationTokenSource.CreateLinkedTokenSource(TestContext.Current.CancellationToken);\n        cancellation.CancelAfter(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(10));\n        var stopwatch = Stopwatch.StartNew();\n        try\n        {\n            await Assert.ThrowsAnyAsync<OperationCanceledException>(() => BoundedProcess.RunAsync(\n                Pwsh(command), TimeSpan.FromMinutes(2), TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2), cancellation.Token));\n\n            Assert.True(stopwatch.Elapsed < TimeSpan.FromSeconds(40), $\"RunAsync returned after {stopwatch.Elapsed}.\");\n            Assert.True(HasExited(pidFile), \"The child outlived the cancellation.\");\n        }\n        finally\n        {\n            KillRecorded(pidFile);\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-004: RunAsync drains standard output and standard error concurrently, so a child that writes 1 MiB to\n    /// standard error (more than any pipe buffer holds) before writing to standard output completes. A reader that drains standard\n    /// output to the end first would leave the child blocked on the full standard error pipe.\n    /// </summary>\n    [Fact]\n    public async Task RunAsync_ChildFillsStandardErrorBeforeWritingOutput_Completes()\n    {\n        var result = await BoundedProcess.RunAsync(\n            Pwsh(\"[Console]::Error.Write([string]::new([char]'e', 1048576)); [Console]::Out.Write('done')\"),\n            TimeSpan.FromMinutes(1),\n            TimeSpan.FromSeconds(10),\n            TestContext.Current.CancellationToken);\n\n        Assert.Equal(0, result.ExitCode);\n        Assert.Equal(\"done\", result.Stdout.Trim());\n        Assert.Equal(1048576, result.Stderr.Count(character => character == 'e'));\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-005: dotnet children ignore persistent build servers, so no MSBuild worker node, MSBuild server, or\n    /// compiler server outlives the child holding its redirected output. Pure start-info construction; no process starts.\n    /// </summary>\n    [Fact]\n    public void Dotnet_AppendsDisableBuildServers()\n    {\n        var startInfo = BoundedProcess.Dotnet(\"repo-root\", [\"build\", \"project.csproj\", \"-c\", \"Debug\"]);\n\n        string[] expected = [\"build\", \"project.csproj\", \"-c\", \"Debug\", \"--disable-build-servers\"];\n        Assert.Equal(\"dotnet\", startInfo.FileName);\n        Assert.Equal(\"repo-root\", startInfo.WorkingDirectory);\n        Assert.Equal(expected, startInfo.ArgumentList);\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-006: no Build.Tests source other than <see cref=\"BoundedProcess\"/> reads a child's redirected output or\n    /// waits for a child to exit, so every child process the suite starts is bounded. Scans the C# sources under tests/Build.Tests\n    /// (build output excluded) for direct output reads and exit waits.\n    /// </summary>\n    [Fact]\n    public void BuildTestsSources_ReadChildOutputOnlyThroughBoundedProcess()\n    {\n        var directory = Path.Combine(FindRepositoryRoot(), \"tests\", \"Build.Tests\");\n        string[] patterns = [\".StandardOutput\", \".StandardError\", \"WaitForExit\", \"BeginOutputReadLine\", \"BeginErrorReadLine\"];\n        string[] owners = [\"BoundedProcess.cs\", \"BoundedProcessTests.cs\"];\n        var offendingLines = Directory.EnumerateFiles(directory, \"*.cs\", SearchOption.AllDirectories)\n            .Where(path => !IsBuildOutput(Path.GetRelativePath(directory, path)))\n            .Where(path => !owners.Contains(Path.GetFileName(path), StringComparer.Ordinal))\n            .SelectMany(path => File.ReadLines(path).Select((line, index) => new { Path = path, Line = line, LineNumber = index + 1 }))\n            .Where(entry => patterns.Any(pattern => entry.Line.Contains(pattern, StringComparison.Ordinal)))\n            .Select(entry => $\"{Path.GetRelativePath(directory, entry.Path)}:{entry.LineNumber}: {entry.Line.Trim()}\")\n            .ToArray();\n\n        Assert.True(\n            offendingLines.Length == 0,\n            \"Read child output and wait for children only through BoundedProcess (TR-MCP-NUKE-009 AC-006):\"\n                + Environment.NewLine\n                + string.Join(Environment.NewLine, offendingLines));\n    }\n\n    private static ProcessStartInfo Pwsh(string command)\n    {\n        var startInfo = new ProcessStartInfo(\"pwsh\");\n        startInfo.ArgumentList.Add(\"-NoLogo\");\n        startInfo.ArgumentList.Add(\"-NoProfile\");\n        startInfo.ArgumentList.Add(\"-NonInteractive\");\n        startInfo.ArgumentList.Add(\"-Command\");\n        startInfo.ArgumentList.Add(command);\n        return startInfo;\n    }\n\n    private static string NewPidFile() => Path.Combine(Path.GetTempPath(), $\"bounded-process-{Guid.NewGuid():N}.pid\");\n\n    private static bool HasExited(string pidFile)\n    {\n        Assert.True(File.Exists(pidFile), \"The child never recorded its process id.\");\n        try\n        {\n            using var process = Process.GetProcessById(int.Parse(File.ReadAllText(pidFile).Trim(), System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture));\n            return process.HasExited;\n        }\n        catch (ArgumentException)\n        {\n            return true;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static void KillRecorded(string pidFile)\n    {\n        if (!File.Exists(pidFile))\n        {\n            return;\n        }\n\n        try\n        {\n            using var process = Process.GetProcessById(int.Parse(File.ReadAllText(pidFile).Trim(), System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture));\n            process.Kill(entireProcessTree: true);\n        }\n        catch (Exception exception) when (exception is ArgumentException or InvalidOperationException or FormatException)\n        {\n        }\n        finally\n        {\n            File.Delete(pidFile);\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static bool IsBuildOutput(string relativePath)\n    {\n        var first = relativePath.Split(Path.DirectorySeparatorChar, Path.AltDirectorySeparatorChar)[0];\n        return first is \"bin\" or \"obj\";\n    }\n\n    private static string FindRepositoryRoot()\n    {\n        var directory = new DirectoryInfo(AppContext.BaseDirectory);\n        while (directory is not null)\n        {\n            if (File.Exists(Path.Combine(directory.FullName, \"QBrainAi.sln\")))\n            {\n                return directory.FullName;\n            }\n\n            directory = directory.Parent;\n        }\n\n        throw new DirectoryNotFoundException(\"Could not find repository root containing QBrainAi.sln.\");\n    }\n}\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\nnamespace NukeBuild.Tests;\n\n/// <summary>\n/// TR-MCP-NUKE-010 (BUG-BUILD-009): verifies that the trim-analysis cleanup removes its artifacts root on every OS. Build-infrastructure\n/// test, accountable through TR only. Uses a temporary directory tree with nested files shaped like a publish output; no mocks.\n/// </summary>\npublic sealed class TrimArtifactCleanupTests\n{\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-NUKE-010 AC-001: <c>TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests.TryDeleteArtifacts</c> removes a populated artifacts root.\n    /// On Windows the delete runs in a detached <c>cmd.exe</c> so an antivirus scan cannot block the test host, so the test polls\n    /// for up to 30 s before asserting.\n    /// </summary>\n    [Fact]\n    public async Task TryDeleteArtifacts_PopulatedRoot_IsRemoved()\n    {\n        var root = Path.Combine(Path.GetTempPath(), \"mcpserver-trim-cleanup-test\", Guid.NewGuid().ToString(\"N\"));\n        Directory.CreateDirectory(Path.Combine(root, \"publish\", \"runtimes\"));\n        await File.WriteAllTextAsync(Path.Combine(root, \"publish\", \"app.dll\"), \"app\", TestContext.Current.CancellationToken);\n        await File.WriteAllTextAsync(Path.Combine(root, \"publish\", \"runtimes\", \"native.so\"), \"native\", TestContext.Current.CancellationToken);\n\n        try\n        {\n            TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests.TryDeleteArtifacts(root);\n\n            var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(30);\n            while (Directory.Exists(root) && DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)\n            {\n                await Task.Delay(TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(200), TestContext.Current.CancellationToken);\n            }\n\n            Assert.False(Directory.Exists(root), $\"TryDeleteArtifacts left {root} in place.\");\n        }\n        finally\n        {\n            if (Directory.Exists(root))\n            {\n                Directory.Delete(root, recursive: true);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command 'Get-Content build/Build.Restore.cs; Get-Content build/Build.Compile.cs; Get-Content build/Build.SyncAgentPlugins.cs; Get-Content build/Build.ValidateConfig.cs' \"","aggregated_output":"using Nuke.Common;\nusing Nuke.Common.Tools.DotNet;\nusing static Nuke.Common.Tools.DotNet.DotNetTasks;\n\npartial class Build\n{\n    /// <summary>Restore NuGet packages for the solution and for every build project outside it (TR-MCP-NUKE-002 AC-003).</summary>\n    public Target Restore => _ => _\n        .Executes(() =>\n        {\n            DotNetRestore(_ => _\n                .SetProjectFile(Solution));\n\n            // Compile builds the whole shared project set with --no-restore, and some of it (the src/Compatibility\n            // aliases) is not in the solution, so restore those projects one by one.\n            var solutionProjects = Solution.GetAllProjects(\"*\")\n                .Select(project => Path.GetFullPath(project.Path))\n                .ToHashSet(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\n            foreach (var projectFile in GetBuildProjectFiles(SourceDirectory, TestsDirectory)\n                         .Where(path => !solutionProjects.Contains(Path.GetFullPath(path))))\n            {\n                DotNetRestore(_ => _\n                    .SetProjectFile(projectFile));\n            }\n        });\n}\nusing Nuke.Common;\nusing Nuke.Common.Tools.DotNet;\nusing static Nuke.Common.Tools.DotNet.DotNetTasks;\n\npartial class Build\n{\n    /// <summary>Compile every project in the shared build project set (TR-MCP-NUKE-002 AC-002).</summary>\n    public Target Compile => _ => _\n        .DependsOn(Restore)\n        .Executes(() =>\n        {\n            var buildVersion = ResolveNuGetPackageVersion(PackageVersion, RootDirectory / \"GitVersion.yml\");\n            var projectFiles = GetBuildProjectFiles(SourceDirectory, TestsDirectory);\n\n            foreach (var projectFile in projectFiles)\n            {\n                DotNetBuild(_ => _\n                    .SetProjectFile(projectFile)\n                    .SetConfiguration(Configuration)\n                    .EnableNoRestore()\n                    .SetProperty(\"PackageVersion\", buildVersion)\n                    .SetProperty(\"Version\", buildVersion)\n                    .SetProperty(\"InformationalVersion\", buildVersion));\n            }\n        });\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-NUKE-002 AC-002: the one project set that Compile builds and Restore restores: every <c>*.csproj</c> under\n    /// <paramref name=\"sourceDirectory\"/> and <paramref name=\"testsDirectory\"/> except <c>Build.Tests</c>, ordered.\n    /// </summary>\n    internal static string[] GetBuildProjectFiles(string sourceDirectory, string testsDirectory) => Directory\n        .EnumerateFiles(sourceDirectory, \"*.csproj\", SearchOption.AllDirectories)\n        .Concat(Directory.EnumerateFiles(testsDirectory, \"*.csproj\", SearchOption.AllDirectories))\n        .Where(path => !path.EndsWith(Path.Combine(\"Build.Tests\", \"Build.Tests.csproj\"), StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n        .OrderBy(path => path, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n        .ToArray();\n}\nusing System.Text.Json;\nusing System.Text.Json.Nodes;\nusing System.Text.RegularExpressions;\nusing Nuke.Common;\nusing Nuke.Common.IO;\nusing Nuke.Common.Tooling;\nusing Serilog;\n\npartial class Build\n{\n    [Parameter(\"Directory containing mcpserver-*-plugin repositories; defaults to the repository parent directory\")]\n    readonly string? AgentPluginParent = null;\n\n    private static readonly JsonSerializerOptions s_pluginJsonOptions = new()\n    {\n        WriteIndented = true\n    };\n\n    private static readonly string[] s_knownAgentPluginRepositories =\n    [\n        \"mcpserver-claude-code-plugin\",\n        \"mcpserver-claude-cowork-plugin\",\n        \"mcpserver-cline-plugin\",\n        \"mcpserver-cline-v2-plugin\",\n        \"mcpserver-codex-plugin\",\n        \"mcpserver-copilot-plugin\",\n        \"mcpserver-grok-plugin\",\n        \"mcpserver-opencode-plugin\"\n    ];\n\n    /// <summary>Sync the canonical plugin core into sibling agent plugins and normalize plugin package versions.</summary>\n    public Target SyncAgentPlugins => _ => _\n        .Executes(() =>\n        {\n            AssertPluginPromotionAllowed();\n\n            var syncScript = RootDirectory / \"plugins\" / \"core\" / \"sync\" / \"sync-plugin-core.ps1\";\n            if (!File.Exists(syncScript.ToString()))\n                throw new FileNotFoundException(\"Plugin core sync script was not found.\", syncScript.ToString());\n\n            var wrapperScript = RootDirectory / \"plugins\" / \"core\" / \"hooks-templates\" / \"generate-wrappers.ps1\";\n            if (!File.Exists(wrapperScript.ToString()))\n                throw new FileNotFoundException(\"Plugin wrapper generator was not found.\", wrapperScript.ToString());\n\n            var stagedRoot = RootDirectory / \"plugins\" / \"core\" / \".staged-plugin\";\n            Directory.CreateDirectory(stagedRoot.ToString());\n            SyncPluginCorePackage(RootDirectory, stagedRoot, syncScript, wrapperScript, \"claude-code\");\n\n            var pluginRoots = DiscoverAgentPluginRoots(RootDirectory, AgentPluginParent);\n            if (pluginRoots.Count == 0)\n            {\n                Log.Warning(\"No known agent plugin repositories were found under {PluginParent}. Synced only the workspace staged plugin package.\", ResolveAgentPluginParentDirectory(RootDirectory, AgentPluginParent));\n                return;\n            }\n\n            foreach (var pluginRoot in pluginRoots)\n            {\n                SyncPluginCorePackage(RootDirectory, pluginRoot, syncScript, wrapperScript, ResolvePluginHostName(pluginRoot));\n            }\n\n            RefreshNodePluginCoreVendorPackages(RootDirectory, pluginRoots);\n\n            var nextVersion = ResolveNextMinorPluginVersion(pluginRoots);\n            var updates = PlanPluginVersionUpdates(pluginRoots, nextVersion);\n            foreach (var update in updates)\n            {\n                File.WriteAllText(update.Path, update.UpdatedContent);\n                Log.Information(\"Updated plugin version in {Path} to {Version}\", update.Path, nextVersion);\n            }\n\n            RefreshKnownPluginCaches(pluginRoots, nextVersion);\n        });\n\n    /// <summary>Validate that generated plugin runtime packages are PowerShell-only.</summary>\n    public Target ValidatePluginPowerShellOnly => _ => _\n        .Executes(() =>\n        {\n            var roots = DiscoverAgentPluginRoots(RootDirectory, AgentPluginParent)\n                .Concat([RootDirectory / \"plugins\" / \"core\" / \".staged-plugin\"])\n                .Where(path => Directory.Exists(path.ToString()))\n                .ToArray();\n\n            foreach (var root in roots)\n                ValidatePluginPowerShellOnlyPackage(root);\n\n            Log.Information(\"PowerShell-only plugin validation passed for {Count} package roots.\", roots.Length);\n        });\n\n    /// <summary>Plan a common minor version bump from the highest version found in plugin manifests and package files.</summary>\n    internal static string ResolveNextMinorPluginVersion(IReadOnlyList<AbsolutePath> pluginRoots)\n    {\n        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(pluginRoots);\n\n        PluginSemanticVersion? highest = null;\n        foreach (var path in EnumerateVersionedFiles(pluginRoots))\n        {\n            foreach (var version in ReadVersionValues(path))\n            {\n                if (!TryParseSemanticVersion(version, out var parsed))\n                    continue;\n\n                if (highest is null || parsed.CompareTo(highest.Value) > 0)\n                    highest = parsed;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (highest is null)\n            throw new InvalidOperationException(\"Could not find a semantic version in plugin manifests or package files.\");\n\n        return $\"{highest.Value.Major}.{highest.Value.Minor + 1}.0\";\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>Create deterministic JSON rewrites for plugin manifests and root package files.</summary>\n    internal static IReadOnlyList<PluginVersionUpdate> PlanPluginVersionUpdates(\n        IReadOnlyList<AbsolutePath> pluginRoots,\n        string version)\n    {\n        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(pluginRoots);\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(version))\n            throw new ArgumentException(\"Plugin version is required.\", nameof(version));\n\n        var updates = new List<PluginVersionUpdate>();\n        foreach (var path in EnumerateVersionedFiles(pluginRoots))\n        {\n            var originalContent = File.ReadAllText(path);\n            var updatedContent = RewriteVersionedFile(path, originalContent, version.Trim());\n            if (!string.Equals(originalContent, updatedContent, StringComparison.Ordinal))\n            {\n                updates.Add(new PluginVersionUpdate(\n                    NormalizePath(path),\n                    originalContent,\n                    updatedContent));\n            }\n        }\n\n        return updates\n            .OrderBy(update => update.Path, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            .ToArray();\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>A planned plugin version file rewrite.</summary>\n    internal sealed record PluginVersionUpdate(string Path, string OriginalContent, string UpdatedContent);\n\n    internal static IReadOnlyList<AbsolutePath> DiscoverAgentPluginRoots(AbsolutePath rootDirectory, string? pluginParent = null)\n    {\n        var parentDirectory = ResolveAgentPluginParentDirectory(rootDirectory, pluginParent);\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(parentDirectory))\n            return [];\n\n        return s_knownAgentPluginRepositories\n            .Select(name => (AbsolutePath)Path.Combine(parentDirectory, name))\n            .Where(path => Directory.Exists(path.ToString()))\n            .OrderBy(path => path.ToString(), StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            .ToArray();\n    }\n\n    internal static string? ResolveAgentPluginParentDirectory(AbsolutePath rootDirectory, string? pluginParent = null)\n    {\n        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(pluginParent))\n            return Path.GetFullPath(pluginParent);\n\n        return ResolveOfficialPluginSiblingParent(rootDirectory.ToString());\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// Resolves the directory that contains official sibling plugin repos.\n    /// Walks up from a git worktree under .worktrees, or under a dot-folder of the checkout such as\n    /// .claude/worktrees or .mcpServer/worktrees, to the checkout parent that holds mcpserver-*-plugin siblings\n    /// (TR-MCP-NUKE-006).\n    /// </summary>\n    internal static string? ResolveOfficialPluginSiblingParent(string rootDirectory)\n    {\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(rootDirectory))\n            return null;\n\n        var current = new DirectoryInfo(Path.GetFullPath(rootDirectory));\n        while (current is not null)\n        {\n            var parent = current.Parent;\n            if (parent is null)\n                break;\n\n            if (Directory.Exists(Path.Combine(parent.FullName, \"mcpserver-codex-plugin\"))\n                || Directory.Exists(Path.Combine(parent.FullName, \"mcpserver-grok-plugin\"))\n                || Directory.Exists(Path.Combine(parent.FullName, \"mcpserver-claude-code-plugin\")))\n            {\n                return parent.FullName;\n            }\n\n            if (string.Equals(current.Name, \".worktrees\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                || string.Equals(current.Name, \"worktrees\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n            {\n                var checkoutRoot = parent;\n                if (checkoutRoot.Name.StartsWith('.'))\n                    checkoutRoot = checkoutRoot.Parent ?? checkoutRoot;\n                return checkoutRoot.Parent?.FullName ?? parent.FullName;\n            }\n\n            current = parent;\n        }\n\n        return Directory.GetParent(Path.GetFullPath(rootDirectory))?.FullName;\n    }\n\n    private static string? ResolvePluginHostName(AbsolutePath pluginRoot)\n    {\n        var repoName = Path.GetFileName(pluginRoot.ToString().TrimEnd(Path.DirectorySeparatorChar, Path.AltDirectorySeparatorChar));\n        return repoName switch\n        {\n            \"mcpserver-claude-code-plugin\" => \"claude-code\",\n            \"mcpserver-claude-cowork-plugin\" => \"claude-cowork\",\n            \"mcpserver-codex-plugin\" => \"codex\",\n            \"mcpserver-copilot-plugin\" => \"copilot\",\n            \"mcpserver-grok-plugin\" => \"grok\",\n            _ => null\n        };\n    }\n\n    private static void SyncPluginCorePackage(\n        AbsolutePath rootDirectory,\n        AbsolutePath pluginRoot,\n        AbsolutePath syncScript,\n        AbsolutePath wrapperScript,\n        string? hostName)\n    {\n        Log.Information(\"Syncing plugin core into {PluginRoot}\", pluginRoot);\n        ProcessTasks.StartProcess(\n                \"pwsh.exe\",\n                $\"-NoLogo -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \\\"{syncScript}\\\" -PluginRoot \\\"{pluginRoot}\\\"\")\n            .AssertZeroExitCode();\n\n        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(hostName))\n        {\n            Log.Information(\"Generating {HostName} PowerShell wrappers in {PluginRoot}\", hostName, pluginRoot);\n            ProcessTasks.StartProcess(\n                    \"pwsh.exe\",\n                    $\"-NoLogo -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \\\"{wrapperScript}\\\" -HostName \\\"{hostName}\\\" -PluginRoot \\\"{pluginRoot}\\\"\")\n                .AssertZeroExitCode();\n        }\n        else\n        {\n            Log.Information(\"No hook wrappers are generated for {PluginRoot}\", pluginRoot);\n        }\n\n        RunPluginCoreIntegrityCheck(rootDirectory, pluginRoot);\n        ValidatePluginPowerShellOnlyPackage(pluginRoot);\n    }\n\n    private static IEnumerable<string> EnumerateVersionedFiles(IReadOnlyList<AbsolutePath> pluginRoots)\n    {\n        foreach (var root in pluginRoots)\n        {\n            var rootPath = root.ToString();\n            if (!Directory.Exists(rootPath))\n                continue;\n\n            var rootVersionFile = Path.Combine(rootPath, \".version\");\n            if (File.Exists(rootVersionFile))\n                yield return rootVersionFile;\n\n            foreach (var file in Directory.EnumerateFiles(rootPath, \"plugin.json\", SearchOption.AllDirectories)\n                         .Concat(Directory.EnumerateFiles(rootPath, \"package.json\", SearchOption.AllDirectories))\n                         .Concat(Directory.EnumerateFiles(rootPath, \"package-lock.json\", SearchOption.AllDirectories))\n                         .Where(IsVersionPlanCandidate)\n                         .OrderBy(path => path, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n            {\n                yield return file;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static bool IsVersionPlanCandidate(string path)\n    {\n        var segments = path.Split(Path.DirectorySeparatorChar, Path.AltDirectorySeparatorChar);\n        if (segments.Any(static segment =>\n                segment.Equals(\".git\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                || segment.Equals(\"bin\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                || segment.Equals(\"obj\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                || segment.Equals(\"cache\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                || segment.Equals(\"node_modules\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)))\n        {\n            return false;\n        }\n\n        var fileName = Path.GetFileName(path);\n        if (fileName.Equals(\"plugin.json\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n            return true;\n\n        return (fileName.Equals(\"package.json\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                || fileName.Equals(\"package-lock.json\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n            && Path.GetDirectoryName(path)?.EndsWith(\"-plugin\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) == true;\n    }\n\n    private static IEnumerable<string> ReadVersionValues(string path)\n    {\n        if (Path.GetFileName(path).Equals(\".version\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n        {\n            var rootVersion = File.ReadAllText(path).Trim();\n            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(rootVersion))\n                yield return rootVersion;\n            yield break;\n        }\n\n        JsonNode? root;\n        try\n        {\n            root = JsonNode.Parse(File.ReadAllText(path));\n        }\n        catch (JsonException)\n        {\n            yield break;\n        }\n\n        if (root is not JsonObject obj)\n            yield break;\n\n        var version = obj[\"version\"]?.GetValue<string>();\n        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(version))\n            yield return version;\n\n        if (Path.GetFileName(path).Equals(\"package-lock.json\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            && obj[\"packages\"]?[\"\"] is JsonObject rootPackage)\n        {\n            var packageVersion = rootPackage[\"version\"]?.GetValue<string>();\n            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(packageVersion))\n                yield return packageVersion;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static string RewriteVersionedFile(string path, string originalContent, string version)\n    {\n        if (Path.GetFileName(path).Equals(\".version\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n            return version + \"\\n\";\n\n        return RewriteVersionedJson(path, originalContent, version);\n    }\n\n    private static string RewriteVersionedJson(string path, string originalContent, string version)\n    {\n        JsonObject root;\n        try\n        {\n            root = JsonNode.Parse(originalContent) as JsonObject\n                ?? throw new InvalidOperationException($\"Expected a JSON object in {path}.\");\n        }\n        catch (JsonException ex)\n        {\n            throw new InvalidOperationException($\"Invalid JSON in plugin version file '{path}': {ex.Message}\", ex);\n        }\n\n        root[\"version\"] = version;\n\n        if (Path.GetFileName(path).Equals(\"package-lock.json\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            && root[\"packages\"]?[\"\"] is JsonObject rootPackage)\n        {\n            rootPackage[\"version\"] = version;\n        }\n\n        var json = root.ToJsonString(s_pluginJsonOptions)\n            .Replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\", StringComparison.Ordinal)\n            .Replace(\"\\r\", \"\\n\", StringComparison.Ordinal);\n        return json + \"\\n\";\n    }\n\n    private static bool TryParseSemanticVersion(string? value, out PluginSemanticVersion version)\n    {\n        version = default;\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(value))\n            return false;\n\n        var core = value.Split(['-', '+'], 2, StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries)[0];\n        var parts = core.Split('.', StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);\n        if (parts.Length < 2 || parts.Length > 3)\n            return false;\n\n        if (!int.TryParse(parts[0], out var major)\n            || !int.TryParse(parts[1], out var minor)\n            || (parts.Length == 3 && !int.TryParse(parts[2], out _)))\n        {\n            return false;\n        }\n\n        var patch = parts.Length == 3 ? int.Parse(parts[2]) : 0;\n        version = new PluginSemanticVersion(major, minor, patch);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    private static void RunPluginCoreIntegrityCheck(AbsolutePath rootDirectory, AbsolutePath pluginRoot)\n    {\n        if (!Directory.Exists(pluginRoot.ToString()))\n            return;\n\n        var script = rootDirectory / \"plugins\" / \"core\" / \"sync\" / \"check-core-integrity.ps1\";\n        if (!File.Exists(script.ToString()))\n        {\n            Log.Warning(\"Plugin core integrity script was not found at {Script}; skipping.\", script);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        ProcessTasks.StartProcess(\n                \"pwsh.exe\",\n                $\"-NoLogo -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \\\"{script}\\\" -PluginRoot \\\"{pluginRoot}\\\"\")\n            .AssertZeroExitCode();\n    }\n\n    private static void ValidatePluginPowerShellOnlyPackage(AbsolutePath pluginRoot)\n    {\n        if (!Directory.Exists(pluginRoot.ToString()))\n            return;\n\n        var forbidden = Directory.EnumerateFiles(pluginRoot.ToString(), \"*\", SearchOption.AllDirectories)\n            .Where(path => !IsUnderIgnoredDirectory(path))\n            .Select(path => new\n            {\n                FullPath = path,\n                Relative = Path.GetRelativePath(pluginRoot.ToString(), path).Replace('\\\\', '/')\n            })\n            .Where(file => !file.Relative.Split('/').Any(static segment => segment.Equals(\"tests\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)))\n            .Where(file => file.Relative.StartsWith(\"lib/\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                || file.Relative.StartsWith(\"hooks/\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                || file.Relative.StartsWith(\"skills/\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                || file.Relative.Equals(\"plugin.json\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                || file.Relative.Equals(\"CORE-MANIFEST.yaml\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n            .Where(file => !file.Relative.Equals(\"bootstrap/install-powershell.sh\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n            .Where(file => HasForbiddenPluginRuntimeReference(file.Relative, file.FullPath))\n            .Select(file => file.Relative)\n            .OrderBy(path => path, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            .ToArray();\n\n        if (forbidden.Length > 0)\n            throw new InvalidOperationException($\"Plugin package {pluginRoot} contains forbidden runtime files or references: {string.Join(\", \", forbidden.Take(20))}\");\n\n        ValidateRequirementsSkillLayerGuidance(pluginRoot.ToString());\n    }\n\n    internal static void ValidateRequirementsSkillLayerGuidance(string pluginRoot)\n    {\n        var skillPath = Path.Combine(pluginRoot, \"skills\", \"requirements\", \"SKILL.md\");\n        if (!File.Exists(skillPath))\n            return;\n\n        var content = File.ReadAllText(skillPath);\n        var requiredFragments = new[]\n        {\n            \"## Requirement Scope Layers\",\n            \"workflow.requirements.listLayers\",\n            \"workflow.requirements.createLayer\",\n            \"workflow.requirements.updateLayer\",\n            \"workflow.requirements.effective\",\n            \"req_list_layers\",\n            \"req_create_layer\",\n            \"req_update_layer\",\n            \"req_effective\",\n            \"client.Requirements.ListRequirementLayersAsync\",\n            \"client.Requirements.CreateRequirementLayerAsync\",\n            \"client.Requirements.UpdateRequirementLayerAsync\",\n            \"client.Requirements.GetEffectiveRequirementsAsync\",\n            \"key\",\n            \"order\",\n            \"name\",\n            \"description\",\n            \"scopeStartLayerKey\",\n            \"scopeEndLayerKey\",\n            \"layerKey\"\n        };\n\n        var missing = requiredFragments\n            .Where(fragment => !content.Contains(fragment, StringComparison.Ordinal))\n            .ToArray();\n\n        if (missing.Length > 0)\n        {\n            throw new InvalidOperationException(\n                $\"Plugin package {pluginRoot} requirements skill is missing requirement layer guidance: {string.Join(\", \", missing)}\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static bool HasForbiddenPluginRuntimeReference(string relative, string fullPath)\n    {\n        if (relative.Contains(\"/lib-sh/\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || relative.Contains(\"/lib-node/\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || relative.EndsWith(\".sh\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || relative.EndsWith(\".bash\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || relative.EndsWith(\".js\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n        {\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        var extension = Path.GetExtension(fullPath);\n        if (!new[] { \".json\", \".md\", \".ps1\", \".psm1\", \".psd1\", \".yaml\", \".yml\", \".txt\" }\n            .Contains(extension, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n        {\n            return false;\n        }\n\n        var content = File.ReadAllText(fullPath);\n        return Regex.IsMatch(\n            content,\n            @\"(\\bbash\\b|\\blib-sh\\b|\\blib-node\\b|(?<!\\$)\\bnode\\s|\\bnode\\.exe\\b|repl-daemon\\.js|complete-turn-to-recovery\\.js|\\.sh\\b|\\.bash\\b|repl-invoke\\.sh|qbrain-ai-repl --agent-stdio|repl_invoke)\",\n            RegexOptions.IgnoreCase);\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-SYNC-001: version-less stable vendor file name, so consumer package.json references\n    /// never break on a version bump and a hard-coded version can never drift from package.json again.\n    /// </summary>\n    const string NodeCoreStableVendorFileName = \"sharpninja-mcpserver-plugin-core.tgz\";\n\n    private static void RefreshNodePluginCoreVendorPackages(\n        AbsolutePath rootDirectory,\n        IReadOnlyList<AbsolutePath> pluginRoots)\n    {\n        // TR-MCP-SYNC-001: discover consumers by ANY tarball variant so first-run migration finds\n        // the legacy version-suffixed files as well as the stable name.\n        var vendorDirectories = pluginRoots\n            .Select(root => root / \"vendor\")\n            .Where(dir => Directory.Exists(dir.ToString())\n                && Directory.GetFiles(dir.ToString(), \"sharpninja-mcpserver-plugin-core*.tgz\").Length > 0)\n            .ToArray();\n        if (vendorDirectories.Length == 0)\n            return;\n\n        var nodeCoreRoot = rootDirectory / \"plugins\" / \"core\" / \"lib-node\";\n        if (!Directory.Exists(nodeCoreRoot.ToString()))\n            throw new DirectoryNotFoundException($\"Node plugin core source was not found at {nodeCoreRoot}.\");\n\n        EnsureNodePluginCoreDependencies(nodeCoreRoot.ToString());\n\n        var manifestVersion = ReadNodeCorePackageVersion(nodeCoreRoot);\n\n        Log.Information(\"Building Node plugin core package for {Count} plugin vendor target(s)\", vendorDirectories.Length);\n        ProcessTasks.StartProcess(\"npm\", \"run build\", workingDirectory: nodeCoreRoot.ToString())\n            .AssertZeroExitCode();\n\n        var pack = ProcessTasks.StartProcess(\n            \"npm\",\n            \"pack --silent\",\n            workingDirectory: nodeCoreRoot.ToString(),\n            logOutput: false);\n        pack.WaitForExit();\n        pack.AssertZeroExitCode();\n\n        var packedFileName = pack.Output\n            .Select(static output => output.Text.Trim())\n            .LastOrDefault(static text => text.EndsWith(\".tgz\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(packedFileName))\n            throw new FileNotFoundException(\"npm pack did not report a packed Node plugin core tarball name.\");\n\n        // TR-MCP-SYNC-001: npm pack derives the tarball name from package.json, so a mismatch here\n        // means the pack ran against a different manifest than the one this sync read. Fail loudly.\n        var expectedPackedFileName = $\"sharpninja-mcpserver-plugin-core-{manifestVersion}.tgz\";\n        if (!string.Equals(packedFileName, expectedPackedFileName, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n        {\n            throw new InvalidOperationException(\n                $\"npm pack produced '{packedFileName}' but plugins/core/lib-node/package.json declares version {manifestVersion} (expected '{expectedPackedFileName}').\");\n        }\n\n        var packedPath = nodeCoreRoot / packedFileName;\n        if (!File.Exists(packedPath.ToString()))\n            throw new FileNotFoundException(\"npm pack did not produce the expected Node plugin core package.\", packedPath.ToString());\n\n        foreach (var vendorDirectory in vendorDirectories)\n        {\n            var stableTarget = vendorDirectory / NodeCoreStableVendorFileName;\n            File.Copy(packedPath.ToString(), stableTarget.ToString(), overwrite: true);\n\n            // Remove superseded variants (the legacy versioned names) so exactly one tarball remains.\n            foreach (var variant in Directory.GetFiles(vendorDirectory.ToString(), \"sharpninja-mcpserver-plugin-core*.tgz\"))\n            {\n                if (!string.Equals(Path.GetFileName(variant), NodeCoreStableVendorFileName, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n                    File.Delete(variant);\n            }\n\n            RewriteVendorDependencyReference(vendorDirectory.Parent);\n            Log.Information(\"Refreshed Node plugin core vendor package {Target} (content {Version})\", stableTarget, manifestVersion);\n        }\n\n        File.Delete(packedPath.ToString());\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>Path to the TypeScript compiler inside plugins/core/lib-node.</summary>\n    /// <param name=\"nodeCoreRoot\">Node plugin core source directory.</param>\n    /// <returns>Expected tsc path under node_modules.</returns>\n    internal static string GetNodePluginCoreTscPath(string nodeCoreRoot)\n        => Path.Combine(nodeCoreRoot, \"node_modules\", \"typescript\", \"bin\", \"tsc\");\n\n    /// <summary>True when plugins/core/lib-node can run <c>tsc</c> from its local TypeScript package.</summary>\n    /// <param name=\"nodeCoreRoot\">Node plugin core source directory.</param>\n    /// <returns>True when typescript/bin/tsc exists.</returns>\n    internal static bool NodePluginCoreHasTsc(string nodeCoreRoot)\n        => File.Exists(GetNodePluginCoreTscPath(nodeCoreRoot));\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// Restores lib-node dependencies with <c>npm ci</c> when typescript/bin/tsc is missing\n    /// so <c>npm run build</c> does not fail with MODULE_NOT_FOUND.\n    /// </summary>\n    /// <param name=\"nodeCoreRoot\">Node plugin core source directory.</param>\n    internal static void EnsureNodePluginCoreDependencies(string nodeCoreRoot)\n    {\n        ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrWhiteSpace(nodeCoreRoot);\n        if (NodePluginCoreHasTsc(nodeCoreRoot))\n            return;\n\n        Log.Information(\"Node plugin core is missing typescript/bin/tsc; running npm ci in {Root}\", nodeCoreRoot);\n        ProcessTasks.StartProcess(\"npm\", \"ci\", workingDirectory: nodeCoreRoot)\n            .AssertZeroExitCode();\n\n        if (!NodePluginCoreHasTsc(nodeCoreRoot))\n        {\n            throw new FileNotFoundException(\n                \"npm ci completed but plugins/core/lib-node/node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc is still missing.\",\n                GetNodePluginCoreTscPath(nodeCoreRoot));\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>Reads the version declared by plugins/core/lib-node/package.json.</summary>\n    /// <param name=\"nodeCoreRoot\">Node plugin core source directory.</param>\n    /// <returns>The manifest version string.</returns>\n    private static string ReadNodeCorePackageVersion(AbsolutePath nodeCoreRoot)\n    {\n        var manifestPath = nodeCoreRoot / \"package.json\";\n        using var manifest = System.Text.Json.JsonDocument.Parse(File.ReadAllText(manifestPath.ToString()));\n        var version = manifest.RootElement.TryGetProperty(\"version\", out var value) ? value.GetString() : null;\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(version))\n            throw new InvalidOperationException($\"package.json at {manifestPath} declares no version.\");\n        return version;\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TR-MCP-SYNC-001: rewrites a consumer's package.json dependency reference from any versioned\n    /// vendor tarball path to the stable version-less name, preserving the file's formatting via a\n    /// targeted in-place replacement.\n    /// </summary>\n    /// <param name=\"pluginRoot\">Consumer plugin repository root containing package.json.</param>\n    private static void RewriteVendorDependencyReference(AbsolutePath pluginRoot)\n    {\n        var packageJsonPath = pluginRoot / \"package.json\";\n        if (!File.Exists(packageJsonPath.ToString()))\n            return;\n\n        var content = File.ReadAllText(packageJsonPath.ToString());\n        var rewritten = Regex.Replace(\n            content,\n            @\"file:vendor/sharpninja-mcpserver-plugin-core[^\"\"]*\\.tgz\",\n            $\"file:vendor/{NodeCoreStableVendorFileName}\");\n        if (!string.Equals(content, rewritten, StringComparison.Ordinal))\n        {\n            File.WriteAllText(packageJsonPath.ToString(), rewritten);\n            Log.Information(\"Rewrote Node core vendor dependency reference in {PackageJson}\", packageJsonPath);\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static void RefreshKnownPluginCaches(IReadOnlyList<AbsolutePath> pluginRoots, string version)\n    {\n        foreach (var pluginRoot in pluginRoots)\n        {\n            foreach (var cacheRoot in ResolvePluginCacheRoots(pluginRoot, version))\n            {\n                ReplacePluginCache(pluginRoot.ToString(), cacheRoot);\n                Log.Information(\"Refreshed plugin cache {CacheRoot}\", cacheRoot);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    internal static void ReplacePluginCache(string sourceRoot, string cacheRoot)\n    {\n        if (HasOpenPluginTurn(cacheRoot))\n        {\n            Log.Information(\n                \"Retaining plugin cache {CacheRoot} because an in-progress turn still references it.\",\n                cacheRoot);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        if (Directory.Exists(cacheRoot))\n        {\n            var parent = Path.GetDirectoryName(cacheRoot)\n                ?? throw new InvalidOperationException($\"Unable to resolve parent directory for plugin cache '{cacheRoot}'.\");\n            Directory.CreateDirectory(parent);\n\n            var oldCacheRoot = Path.Combine(\n                parent,\n                $\"{Path.GetFileName(cacheRoot)}.deleting-{DateTime.UtcNow:yyyyMMddHHmmssfff}\");\n\n            Directory.Move(cacheRoot, oldCacheRoot);\n            if (!TryDeletePluginCacheDirectory(oldCacheRoot, out var cleanupError))\n                Log.Warning(cleanupError, \"Could not remove old plugin cache {CacheRoot}; continuing after replacement.\", oldCacheRoot);\n        }\n\n        CopyDirectory(sourceRoot, cacheRoot);\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// TEST-MCP-TRIAGEPLUGIN-002: true when cacheRoot (or a child session folder)\n    /// still has a current-turn.yaml with status in_progress.\n    /// </summary>\n    internal static bool HasOpenPluginTurn(string cacheRoot)\n    {\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(cacheRoot) || !Directory.Exists(cacheRoot))\n            return false;\n\n        var turnFiles = new List<string>();\n        var rootTurn = Path.Combine(cacheRoot, \"current-turn.yaml\");\n        if (File.Exists(rootTurn))\n            turnFiles.Add(rootTurn);\n\n        var sessionsDir = Path.Combine(cacheRoot, \"sessions\");\n        if (Directory.Exists(sessionsDir))\n        {\n            turnFiles.AddRange(Directory.EnumerateFiles(\n                sessionsDir,\n                \"current-turn.yaml\",\n                SearchOption.AllDirectories));\n        }\n\n        foreach (var turnFile in turnFiles)\n        {\n            var text = File.ReadAllText(turnFile);\n            if (text.Contains(\"status: in_progress\", StringComparison.Ordinal)\n                || text.Contains(\"status:in_progress\", StringComparison.Ordinal))\n            {\n                return true;\n            }\n        }\n\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    internal static bool TryDeletePluginCacheDirectory(string cacheRoot, out Exception? error)\n    {\n        error = null;\n        if (!Directory.Exists(cacheRoot))\n            return true;\n\n        try\n        {\n            var options = new EnumerationOptions\n            {\n                AttributesToSkip = 0,\n                IgnoreInaccessible = true,\n                RecurseSubdirectories = true\n            };\n\n            foreach (var path in Directory.EnumerateFileSystemEntries(cacheRoot, \"*\", options))\n                File.SetAttributes(path, FileAttributes.Normal);\n\n            File.SetAttributes(cacheRoot, FileAttributes.Normal);\n            Directory.Delete(cacheRoot, recursive: true);\n            return true;\n        }\n        catch (Exception ex) when (ex is IOException or UnauthorizedAccessException)\n        {\n            error = ex;\n            return false;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static IEnumerable<string> ResolvePluginCacheRoots(AbsolutePath pluginRoot, string version)\n    {\n        var home = Environment.GetFolderPath(Environment.SpecialFolder.UserProfile);\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(home))\n            return [];\n\n        return ResolvePluginCacheRoots(pluginRoot, version, home);\n    }\n\n    internal static IReadOnlyList<string> ResolvePluginCacheRoots(\n        AbsolutePath pluginRoot,\n        string version,\n        string homeDirectory)\n    {\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(homeDirectory))\n            return [];\n\n        var roots = new List<string>();\n        var repoName = Path.GetFileName(pluginRoot.ToString().TrimEnd(Path.DirectorySeparatorChar, Path.AltDirectorySeparatorChar));\n        if (repoName.Equals(\"mcpserver-codex-plugin\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n        {\n            roots.Add(Path.Combine(homeDirectory, \".codex\", \"plugins\", \"cache\", \"mcpserver-codex-plugin\", \"mcpserver\", version));\n            roots.Add(Path.Combine(homeDirectory, \".codex\", \"plugins\", \"cache\", \"mcpserver-local\", \"mcpserver\", version));\n        }\n\n        if (repoName.Equals(\"mcpserver-claude-code-plugin\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n            roots.Add(Path.Combine(homeDirectory, \".claude\", \"plugins\", \"cache\", \"mcpserver-local\", \"mcpserver\", version));\n\n        if (repoName.Equals(\"mcpserver-claude-cowork-plugin\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n            roots.Add(Path.Combine(homeDirectory, \".claude\", \"plugins\", \"cache\", \"mcpserver-cowork\", \"mcpserver-cowork\", version));\n\n        if (repoName.Equals(\"mcpserver-cline-plugin\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || repoName.Equals(\"mcpserver-cline-v2-plugin\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n        {\n            var clineLocalRoot = Path.Combine(homeDirectory, \".cline\", \"plugins\", \"_installed\", \"local\");\n            if (Directory.Exists(clineLocalRoot))\n            {\n                roots.AddRange(Directory.EnumerateDirectories(clineLocalRoot, repoName + \"-*\", SearchOption.TopDirectoryOnly)\n                    .Select(path => Path.Combine(path, \"package\")));\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (repoName.Equals(\"mcpserver-grok-plugin\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n        {\n            var grokInstalledRoot = Path.Combine(homeDirectory, \".grok\", \"installed-plugins\");\n            if (Directory.Exists(grokInstalledRoot))\n            {\n                roots.AddRange(Directory.EnumerateDirectories(grokInstalledRoot, \"*mcpserver-grok-plugin*\", SearchOption.TopDirectoryOnly));\n            }\n        }\n\n        return roots\n            .Distinct(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            .OrderBy(path => path, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            .ToArray();\n    }\n\n    private static void CopyDirectory(string sourceRoot, string destinationRoot)\n    {\n        Directory.CreateDirectory(destinationRoot);\n\n        foreach (var directory in Directory.EnumerateDirectories(sourceRoot, \"*\", SearchOption.AllDirectories)\n                     .Where(path => !IsUnderIgnoredDirectory(path)))\n        {\n            Directory.CreateDirectory(Path.Combine(destinationRoot, Path.GetRelativePath(sourceRoot, directory)));\n        }\n\n        foreach (var file in Directory.EnumerateFiles(sourceRoot, \"*\", SearchOption.AllDirectories)\n                     .Where(path => !IsUnderIgnoredDirectory(path)))\n        {\n            var relativePath = Path.GetRelativePath(sourceRoot, file);\n            var destination = Path.Combine(destinationRoot, relativePath);\n            Directory.CreateDirectory(Path.GetDirectoryName(destination)!);\n            File.Copy(file, destination, overwrite: true);\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static bool IsUnderIgnoredDirectory(string path)\n    {\n        var segments = path.Split(Path.DirectorySeparatorChar, Path.AltDirectorySeparatorChar);\n        return segments.Any(static segment =>\n            segment.Equals(\".git\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || segment.Equals(\"node_modules\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || segment.Equals(\"tests\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || segment.Equals(\"test-fixtures\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || segment.Equals(\"lib-sh\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || segment.Equals(\"lib-node\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || segment.Equals(\"bin\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n            || segment.Equals(\"obj\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));\n    }\n\n    private static string NormalizePath(string path) => path.Replace('\\\\', '/');\n\n    private readonly record struct PluginSemanticVersion(int Major, int Minor, int Patch)\n        : IComparable<PluginSemanticVersion>\n    {\n        public int CompareTo(PluginSemanticVersion other)\n        {\n            var major = Major.CompareTo(other.Major);\n            if (major != 0)\n                return major;\n\n            var minor = Minor.CompareTo(other.Minor);\n            if (minor != 0)\n                return minor;\n\n            return Patch.CompareTo(other.Patch);\n        }\n    }\n}\nusing Nuke.Common;\nusing Serilog;\n\npartial class Build\n{\n    /// <summary>Validate MCP appsettings instance configuration.</summary>\n    public Target ValidateConfig => _ => _\n        .Executes(() =>\n        {\n            string[] candidatePaths =\n            [\n                SourceDirectory / \"QBrainAi.Support.Mcp\" / \"appsettings.yaml\",\n                SourceDirectory / \"QBrainAi.Support.Mcp\" / \"appsettings.yml\",\n                SourceDirectory / \"QBrainAi.Support.Mcp\" / \"appsettings.json\",\n            ];\n\n            var configPath = candidatePaths.FirstOrDefault(File.Exists)\n                ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\"No appsettings file found.\");\n\n            var lines = File.ReadAllLines(configPath);\n            var instances = ConfigValidator.ParseInstances(lines)\n                ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\"Missing 'QBrainAi' (or legacy 'Mcp') section in config.\");\n\n            if (instances.Count == 0)\n            {\n                Log.Information(\"No Mcp:Instances configured. Validation passed.\");\n                return;\n            }\n\n            var errors = ConfigValidator.Validate(instances);\n            foreach (var error in errors)\n                Log.Error(error);\n\n            if (errors.Count > 0)\n                throw new InvalidOperationException($\"Config validation failed with {errors.Count} error(s).\");\n\n            Log.Information(\"MCP config validation passed for {Count} instances.\", instances.Count);\n        });\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
