{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command '\"'$env:MCP_WORKSPACE_PATH=\"/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer\"; $w=\"/home/sharpninja/.codex/plugins/cache/mcpserver-codex-plugin/mcpserver/1.118.0/Invoke-CodexMcpPlugin.ps1\"; & $w -Command Invoke -Method workflow.todo.get -ParamsObject @{id=\"BUG-BUILD-007\"} -CacheRoot \"/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/session-20261009/.mcpServer/codex\"'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"type: result\npayload:\n  requestId: req-20261010T225701Z-5086\n  result:\n    id: BUG-BUILD-007\n    title: Bound the dotnet build child waits in Build.Tests so a lingering build server cannot hang the suite\n    section: Build\n    priority: high\n    done: false\n    description:\n    - 'MigrationAssemblyObsoleteWarningTests.MigrationAssemblies_CompileSuccessfully hangs the Build.Tests infrastructure suite: RunDotnetBuildAsync (tests/Build.Tests/MigrationAssemblyObsoleteWarningTests.cs:136-160) awaits stdout and stderr EOF and process exit of a dotnet build child with no timeout and no node-reuse or build-server guard. RequirementsWikiPublishScriptTests.cs:134 and YamlObjectMutationTests.cs:132 wait the same way.'\n    - 'Two full Build.Tests runs on 2026-10-10 in worktree .claude/worktrees/session-20261009 (Linux, SDK 10.0.201) stalled with an idle test host: the first was stopped by hand after 26 minutes (343 of 354 tests reported), the second was killed by --blame-hang-timeout 10m (346 of 354 reported). The blame sequence file lists exactly one started-but-not-completed test: NukeBuild.Tests.MigrationAssemblyObsoleteWarningTests.MigrationAssemblies_CompileSuccessfully. The same suite completed in about 4 minutes that morning.'\n    - 'Triage: triage-report-c381e4c99d284e0dbc1ec443c221ca59.'\n    - 'Classification: Build.Tests is the build-infrastructure suite, not application unit tests (operator ruling 2026-10-10T17:30:54Z); accountability through a TR only (operator ruling 2026-10-10T17:32:03Z: \"NUKE is only accountable through TR.\"). BUG-BUILD-001 and BUG-BUILD-002 need this suite fully green, so this blocks their HV.'\n    - 'Fix by Byrd v4: root cause with evidence (confirm or refute the inherited-pipe hypothesis), a RED case that reproduces the unbounded wait, the fix (bounded wait and no lingering build servers holding the pipes), green with zero skips and the full suite completing, then a Codex gpt-6-sol xhigh HV before done.'\n    - \"Root cause observed live on 2026-10-10 at 22:14Z (Linux, SDK 10.0.201) during the BUG-BUILD-006 trim-inventory run: the Build.Tests process (PID 2575389, 0 s CPU over 850 s, no child processes) was blocked on EOF of a dotnet child that had already exited; the other ends of both redirected pipes (pipe:[16191191] stdout, pipe:[16191192] stderr) were held as fd 1 and fd 2 by an MSBuild worker node (MSBuild.dll /nodemode:1 /nodeReuse:true, PID 2575659) that the child's build had spawned and that had been reparented to the user systemd (PPID 1082); the node also held the test process's stdin. Node reuse keeps such a node alive after the build, so EOF never arrives; when an idle reusable node already exists the build connects to it instead and nothing inherits the pipes, which explains the earlier passing run. TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests bounds only WaitForExitAsync (20 minutes); the await of its output tasks that follows is unbounded. Receipt: bug-build-007-evidence.log.txt.\"\n    - 'Call sites with an unbounded wait on redirected child output (6, not 3): MigrationAssemblyObsoleteWarningTests.RunDotnetBuildAsync (dotnet build; the observed suite hang), TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests.RunDotnetAsync (dotnet build and publish; exit bounded at 20 minutes, output unbounded; hung live), RequirementsWikiPublishScriptTests.RunScriptAsync (pwsh; reads stdout to the end before stderr, which can also deadlock on a full stderr pipe), YamlObjectMutationTests.RunPowerShellAsync (pwsh), ServiceUpdateTests.Native and the ServiceUpdateTests fixture tar runner (exit bounded at 30 s, then an unbounded Task.WaitAll on the output).'\n    technicalDetails: &o0 []\n    implementationTasks:\n    - task: \"Root cause with live evidence (bug-build-007-evidence.log.txt): an MSBuild worker node spawned with node reuse by the child's build inherits and holds its stdout and stderr; TR-MCP-NUKE-009 created under FR-MCP-BUILD-001\"\n      done: true\n    - task: 'RED: BoundedProcessTests against a stub with the unbounded pattern: Failed 5, Passed 1, Skipped 0 (held-output case waited 30 s, timeout case 60 s, cancelled child outlived the cancellation, --disable-build-servers missing, source guard listed the six call sites); the concurrent-drain case passes as a characterization test'\n      done: true\n    - task: 'Fix (7d0c299e): BoundedProcess for all six call sites, --disable-build-servers on dotnet children; BoundedProcessTests Passed 6, Skipped 0; full Build.Tests in the default environment completed in 4 m 20 s (Failed 2, Passed 362, Skipped 0; the two failures are BUG-BUILD-008); no MSBuild worker node left running. Receipts: docs/receipts/bug-build-003-009-20261010T224959Z.md (c34d10c4)'\n      done: true\n    - task: Codex gpt-6-sol xhigh HV pass before done\n      done: false\n    dependsOn: *o0\n    functionalRequirements: *o0\n    technicalRequirements: *o0\n  deprecated: true\n\n---\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
