{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command 'Get-ChildItem /tmp/hv-build-store -Filter \\\"BUG-BUILD-*.yaml\\\" | Sort-Object Name | ForEach-Object { \"'$t=Get-Content -Raw $_.FullName; $req=[regex]::Match($t,\"(?ms)''^    technicalRequirements:.*?(?=''^  deprecated:|'\"\\\\z)\\\").Value.Trim(); \"'$i=([regex]::Matches($t,\"(?m)''^    - task:\")).Count; $d=([regex]::Matches($t,\"(?m)''^      done: true$\")).Count; \"{0}: tasks {1}/{2}; {3}\" -f $_.BaseName,$d,$i,($req -replace \"`n\",\" \") }; Get-ChildItem /tmp/hv-build-store -Filter \"TR-MCP-*.yaml\" | Sort-Object Name | ForEach-Object { $t=Get-Content -Raw $_.FullName; \"`n=== $($_.BaseName) ===\"; $t -split \"`n\" | Where-Object {$_ -match \"''^    (id:|title:|description:|status:|text:|evidence:|isSatisfied:)\"} }'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"BUG-BUILD-001: tasks 3/5; technicalRequirements: *o0\nBUG-BUILD-002: tasks 3/5; technicalRequirements: *o0\nBUG-BUILD-003: tasks 3/4; technicalRequirements: *o0\nBUG-BUILD-004: tasks 3/4; technicalRequirements: *o0\nBUG-BUILD-005: tasks 3/4; technicalRequirements: *o0\nBUG-BUILD-006: tasks 3/4; technicalRequirements: *o0\nBUG-BUILD-007: tasks 3/4; technicalRequirements: *o0\nBUG-BUILD-008: tasks 0/4; technicalRequirements: *o0\nBUG-BUILD-009: tasks 3/5; technicalRequirements: *o0\n\n=== TR-MCP-NUKE-002 ===\n    id: TR-MCP-NUKE-002\n    title: Nuke solution parameter and shared build project set\n    description: 'The checked-in .nuke/parameters.json SHALL name a solution file that exists at the repository root, so Nuke can inject Build.Solution and every ./build.ps1 target that depends on Restore can run. The Nuke Compile target SHALL build, and the Restore target SHALL restore, one shared project set: every *.csproj under src/ and tests/ except tests/Build.Tests, as returned by Build.GetBuildProjectFiles. Restore SHALL restore the solution and then each project of that set that the solution does not list, so the --no-restore builds of Compile never fail with NETSDK1004.'\n    status: pending\n\n=== TR-MCP-NUKE-006 ===\n    id: TR-MCP-NUKE-006\n    title: Sibling plugin parent resolution from the checkout or its worktrees\n    description: 'Build.ResolveOfficialPluginSiblingParent, the default plugin parent for SyncAgentPlugins and the plugin-core checksum checks, SHALL return the directory that holds the mcpserver-*-plugin repositories when run from the main checkout or from a git worktree of it: a .worktrees/<name> worktree inside the checkout, or a worktree under a dot-folder of the checkout such as .claude/worktrees/<name> (Claude Code) or .mcpServer/worktrees/<name>.'\n    status: pending\n\n=== TR-MCP-NUKE-007 ===\n    id: TR-MCP-NUKE-007\n    title: InstallReplTool detects the installed REPL global tool by its package id\n    description: The Nuke InstallReplTool target SHALL read the installed version of the QBrainAI.Repl global tool (command qbrain-ai-repl) from dotnet tool list --global by package id, case-insensitively, so it updates or skips correctly; the 1.x alias package SharpNinja.McpServer.Repl (command mcpserver-repl, TR-MCP-QBRAIN-003) is a different tool and never satisfies a QBrainAI.Repl lookup.\n    status: pending\n\n=== TR-MCP-NUKE-008 ===\n    id: TR-MCP-NUKE-008\n    title: ValidateConfig reads the canonical QBrainAi root and the legacy Mcp root\n    description: 'The Nuke ConfigValidator (./build.ps1 ValidateConfig, the G5 configuration check) SHALL parse instance configuration under the canonical QBrainAi: root of appsettings.yaml and under the legacy Mcp: root, as the server itself does through CanonicalSectionProjectionProvider, and SHALL report a missing root naming both.'\n    status: pending\n\n=== TR-MCP-NUKE-009 ===\n    id: TR-MCP-NUKE-009\n    title: Build infrastructure tests bound every child process and its redirected output\n    description: Every child process that the Build.Tests infrastructure suite starts with redirected standard output and standard error SHALL run through one shared helper that bounds the wait for the child to exit, bounds the wait for its redirected output to close after it exits, drains both streams concurrently, kills the child's process tree when the exit timeout expires or the caller cancels, and starts dotnet children with --disable-build-servers, so that no child, descendant, or persistent build server can stall the suite.\n    status: pending\n\n=== TR-MCP-NUKE-010 ===\n    id: TR-MCP-NUKE-010\n    title: Build infrastructure tests remove their temporary build artifacts on every OS\n    description: A Build.Tests case that builds or publishes into a temporary artifacts root SHALL remove that root when it finishes, on Linux, macOS, and Windows. On Windows the removal SHALL NOT block the test host, because an antivirus scan of a trimmed self-contained publish tree can hold a recursive delete for tens of minutes.\n    status: pending\n\n=== TR-MCP-QUALITY-001 ===\n    id: TR-MCP-QUALITY-001\n    title: Warning suppression decision register and aiUnit audit\n    description: >-\n    status: pending\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
