{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command 'foreach(\"'$id in @(\"TR-MCP-NUKE-002\",\"TR-MCP-NUKE-006\",\"TR-MCP-NUKE-007\",\"TR-MCP-NUKE-008\",\"TR-MCP-NUKE-010\",\"TR-MCP-QUALITY-001\")){ \"=== $id ===\"; Get-Content \"/tmp/hv-build-store/$id.yaml\" | Select-Object -Skip 5 -First 90 }'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"=== TR-MCP-NUKE-002 ===\n    title: Nuke solution parameter and shared build project set\n    description: 'The checked-in .nuke/parameters.json SHALL name a solution file that exists at the repository root, so Nuke can inject Build.Solution and every ./build.ps1 target that depends on Restore can run. The Nuke Compile target SHALL build, and the Restore target SHALL restore, one shared project set: every *.csproj under src/ and tests/ except tests/Build.Tests, as returned by Build.GetBuildProjectFiles. Restore SHALL restore the solution and then each project of that set that the solution does not list, so the --no-restore builds of Compile never fail with NETSDK1004.'\n    status: pending\n    priority: high\n    area: MCP\n    subarea: NUKE\n    notes: 'Implementation detail of FR-MCP-BUILD-001 \"Tooling for repeatable builds\" (operator, 2026-10-10: \"FR: Project will provide tooling for repeatable builds.\" / \"Now, the TR are implementation detail of the FR.\"); Nuke behavior is accountable only through TRs (\"NUKE is only accountable through TR.\"), and it maps to no application FR and has no TEST record. Verified by the Build.Tests infrastructure suite, which is not a unit-test suite. Introduced for BUG-BUILD-001 (triage-report-5b07fc9222b543b0810889bc9fcc31e2) and BUG-BUILD-002 (triage-report-fed753f7ec23496893a8bae0de0fefcc) under P0.1 of PLAN-SESSIONTURNREVIEW-001. ACs are satisfied when those TODOs pass their Codex HV.'\n    acceptanceCriteria:\n    - id: AC-001\n      text: .nuke/parameters.json names a solution file that exists at the repository root.\n      isSatisfied: false\n      evidence: tests/Build.Tests/NukeParametersTests.cs (NukeParameters_Solution_NamesExistingSolutionFile)\n    - id: AC-002\n      text: Build.GetBuildProjectFiles returns every *.csproj under src/ and tests/ except tests/Build.Tests, ordered by path (OrdinalIgnoreCase), and Compile builds exactly that set.\n      isSatisfied: false\n      evidence: tests/Build.Tests/BuildProjectSetTests.cs (GetBuildProjectFiles_CoversEverySourceAndTestProject_ExceptBuildTests, RestoreAndCompile_UseTheSharedProjectSet); tests/Build.Tests/BuildTargetTests.cs (BuildTargets_UseGitVersionForCompileAndReplTool)\n    - id: AC-003\n      text: Restore restores the solution and then every project of the shared set that the solution does not list, so ./build.ps1 Compile succeeds with no NETSDK1004.\n      isSatisfied: false\n      evidence: tests/Build.Tests/BuildProjectSetTests.cs (RestoreAndCompile_UseTheSharedProjectSet); ./build.ps1 Compile and ./build.ps1 Test receipts under docs/receipts/\n    scopeStartLayerKey: layer-1\n    createdAt: 2026-10-10T22:58:46.7519413+00:00\n    updatedAt: 2026-10-10T22:58:46.7520627+00:00\n  deprecated: true\n\n---\n\n=== TR-MCP-NUKE-006 ===\n    title: Sibling plugin parent resolution from the checkout or its worktrees\n    description: 'Build.ResolveOfficialPluginSiblingParent, the default plugin parent for SyncAgentPlugins and the plugin-core checksum checks, SHALL return the directory that holds the mcpserver-*-plugin repositories when run from the main checkout or from a git worktree of it: a .worktrees/<name> worktree inside the checkout, or a worktree under a dot-folder of the checkout such as .claude/worktrees/<name> (Claude Code) or .mcpServer/worktrees/<name>.'\n    status: pending\n    priority: high\n    area: MCP\n    subarea: NUKE\n    notes: 'Implementation detail of FR-MCP-BUILD-001 \"Tooling for repeatable builds\" (operator, 2026-10-10: \"Now, the TR are implementation detail of the FR.\"; \"NUKE is only accountable through TR.\"); no TEST record. Introduced for BUG-BUILD-003 (triage-report-75290be6d6b749119a7819fba3cca386): from .claude/worktrees/<name> the walk stopped at the worktrees folder and stepped up only past .mcpServer, returning the McpServer checkout instead of its parent.'\n    acceptanceCriteria:\n    - id: AC-001\n      text: From <parent>/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/<name>, <parent>/McpServer/.mcpServer/worktrees/<name>, and <parent>/<repo>/.worktrees/<name>, ResolveOfficialPluginSiblingParent returns <parent>.\n      isSatisfied: false\n      evidence: tests/Build.Tests/PluginParentResolutionTests.cs\n    - id: AC-002\n      text: The plugin-core checksum checks find the official plugin repositories when run from a .claude/worktrees worktree.\n      isSatisfied: false\n      evidence: tests/Build.Tests/SyncAgentPluginsChecksumTests.cs; tests/Build.Tests/DocsSyncG8OverlayTests.cs\n    scopeStartLayerKey: layer-1\n    createdAt: 2026-10-10T22:58:51.2280997+00:00\n    updatedAt: 2026-10-10T22:58:51.2282860+00:00\n  deprecated: true\n\n---\n\n=== TR-MCP-NUKE-007 ===\n    title: InstallReplTool detects the installed REPL global tool by its package id\n    description: The Nuke InstallReplTool target SHALL read the installed version of the QBrainAI.Repl global tool (command qbrain-ai-repl) from dotnet tool list --global by package id, case-insensitively, so it updates or skips correctly; the 1.x alias package SharpNinja.McpServer.Repl (command mcpserver-repl, TR-MCP-QBRAIN-003) is a different tool and never satisfies a QBrainAI.Repl lookup.\n    status: pending\n    priority: medium\n    area: MCP\n    subarea: NUKE\n    notes: \"Implementation detail of FR-MCP-BUILD-001 \\\"Tooling for repeatable builds\\\" (operator, 2026-10-10: \\\"Now, the TR are implementation detail of the FR.\\\"); package ids per TR-MCP-QBRAIN-003. Introduced for BUG-BUILD-004 (triage-report-dbbbec24a03a4d70856cfe9c5fd7ab80): the rename commit 6de989f3 changed the test sample's command and lookup id but left the package id column at sharpninja.mcpserver.repl.\"\n    acceptanceCriteria:\n    - id: AC-001\n      text: Given dotnet tool list --global output with qbrainai.repl 6.1.1 (qbrain-ai-repl) and sharpninja.mcpserver.repl 1.4.41 (mcpserver-repl), GetInstalledGlobalToolVersion returns 6.1.1 for QBrainAI.Repl, 1.4.41 for SharpNinja.McpServer.Repl, and null for a missing tool.\n      isSatisfied: false\n      evidence: tests/Build.Tests/BuildTargetTests.cs (InstallReplTool_ParsesInstalledGlobalToolVersion)\n    scopeStartLayerKey: layer-1\n    createdAt: 2026-10-10T22:58:53.8650321+00:00\n    updatedAt: 2026-10-10T22:58:53.8651600+00:00\n  deprecated: true\n\n---\n\n=== TR-MCP-NUKE-008 ===\n    title: ValidateConfig reads the canonical QBrainAi root and the legacy Mcp root\n    description: 'The Nuke ConfigValidator (./build.ps1 ValidateConfig, the G5 configuration check) SHALL parse instance configuration under the canonical QBrainAi: root of appsettings.yaml and under the legacy Mcp: root, as the server itself does through CanonicalSectionProjectionProvider, and SHALL report a missing root naming both.'\n    status: pending\n    priority: high\n    area: MCP\n    subarea: NUKE\n    notes: \"Implementation detail of FR-MCP-BUILD-001 \\\"Tooling for repeatable builds\\\" (operator, 2026-10-10: \\\"Now, the TR are implementation detail of the FR.\\\"). Introduced for BUG-BUILD-005 (triage-report-dbbbec24a03a4d70856cfe9c5fd7ab80): after the QBrainAi rename the live appsettings.yaml root is QBrainAi: (line 46), but McpSectionRegex matched only ^Mcp:, so ParseInstances returned null and ./build.ps1 ValidateConfig threw \\\"Missing 'Mcp' section in config.\\\", failing G5.\"\n    acceptanceCriteria:\n    - id: AC-001\n      text: 'ParseInstances returns the instances under a QBrainAi: root and under a legacy Mcp: root, and null when neither root is present.'\n      isSatisfied: false\n      evidence: tests/Build.Tests/ConfigValidatorTests.cs\n    - id: AC-002\n      text: The shipped validator parses and validates the live src/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp/appsettings.yaml without errors, and ./build.ps1 ValidateConfig succeeds.\n      isSatisfied: false\n      evidence: tests/Build.Tests/DocsSyncG8OverlayTests.cs (G8_ValidateConfig_ShippedValidator_PassesOnLiveAppsettings); ./build.ps1 ValidateConfig\n    scopeStartLayerKey: layer-1\n    createdAt: 2026-10-10T22:58:56.3421149+00:00\n    updatedAt: 2026-10-10T22:58:56.3422524+00:00\n  deprecated: true\n\n---\n\n=== TR-MCP-NUKE-010 ===\n    title: Build infrastructure tests remove their temporary build artifacts on every OS\n    description: A Build.Tests case that builds or publishes into a temporary artifacts root SHALL remove that root when it finishes, on Linux, macOS, and Windows. On Windows the removal SHALL NOT block the test host, because an antivirus scan of a trimmed self-contained publish tree can hold a recursive delete for tens of minutes.\n    status: pending\n    priority: high\n    area: MCP\n    subarea: NUKE\n    notes: 'Implementation detail of FR-MCP-BUILD-001 \"Tooling for repeatable builds\" (operator, 2026-10-10: \"Now, the TR are implementation detail of the FR.\"). Introduced for BUG-BUILD-009 (triage-report-410efece19aa4877931d88b4aa9f0928): TrimAnalysisWarningInventoryTests.TryDeleteArtifacts (added in 55fae924) deletes only through a detached cmd.exe /c rmdir; Linux and macOS have no cmd.exe, the Win32Exception is swallowed, and every trim-inventory run leaked eight artifact trees (38 run directories, 4.0 GB, in a tmpfs /tmp on LAB-OMARCHY by 2026-10-10).'\n    acceptanceCriteria:\n    - id: AC-001\n      text: TryDeleteArtifacts removes a populated artifacts root on Linux, macOS, and Windows; on Windows it keeps the non-blocking detached delete.\n      isSatisfied: false\n      evidence: tests/Build.Tests/TrimArtifactCleanupTests.cs\n    scopeStartLayerKey: layer-1\n    createdAt: 2026-10-10T22:59:01.5723449+00:00\n    updatedAt: 2026-10-10T22:59:01.5724749+00:00\n  deprecated: true\n\n---\n\n=== TR-MCP-QUALITY-001 ===\n    title: Warning suppression decision register and aiUnit audit\n    description: >-\n      Warning remediation must distinguish approved suppressions from required fixes through structured acceptance criteria, durable TODO state, suppression inventory validation, and a dedicated aiUnit governance review.\n\n      **Covered by:** FR: FR-MCP-139; TEST: TEST-MCP-AIUNIT-002\n    status: pending\n    priority: medium\n    area: MCP\n    subarea: QUALITY\n    acceptanceCriteria: []\n    scopeStartLayerKey: layer-1\n    createdAt: 2026-10-10T22:59:04.1701888+00:00\n    updatedAt: 2026-10-10T22:59:04.1703130+00:00\n  deprecated: true\n\n---\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
